WEBVTT

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:29.680
historical city of commerce and tradition.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:37.050
Once a year, travelers from the four corners of the world come to see and marvel at the far-famed International Festival,

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:40.390
which is dedicated to the highest and purest ideals in art.

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:45.710
Occasionally, well, something like this slips in.

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:50.360
I'm deeply honored. In fact, I'm at a loss for work.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:52.600
And we're at a loss for money. Our money.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:55.540
Now, please, please, I know that I haven't paid a few small bills, but...

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:58.970
Listen to me, Frost. There are two men back there loading up my scenery into a van.

00:01:59.150 --> 00:01:59.970
And unless they get the...

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:04.260
Now, Mr. Janskul, if you take back your scenery, I can't open.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:06.120
If I can't open, no one will be paid.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:08.680
Now, your only chance, all of you, is to let me open.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:10.640
It isn't the money, Mr. Frost. It's the principal.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:11.880
Hey, the principal.

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:16.060
Uh, you, uh, you don't want the money?

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:17.540
No. Yes!

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:20.890
Ah, the government will get the most of that anyway.

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:24.050
A noble sentiment, Mr. Janskul. That's just my point.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.770
Now, look at these poor little girls.

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:27.910
Open up, Charlie.

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:28.790
Come on, Pat, open them up.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:32.790
Ladies and gentlemen, these are all hard-working young girls.

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:34.830
Each one an artist, a star in the making.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:36.660
Well, think of their careers.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:38.840
My creditors, I appeal to you.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.340
I came from America to add my humble talents to your magnificent festival.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:45.240
From all over the world, people are flocking to this wonderful city.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:47.640
Do you think they will dare to miss frolics to you?

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:49.860
What a performance.

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:52.270
It gets better and better.

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:54.530
Please, I beg of you, give me more time.

00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:56.380
How much time do you want?

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:58.600
Give me three days.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:02:59.760
Three days.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.320
No, no, no, no.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:04.870
Right. We'll give you 48 hours.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.120
My predators, I love you.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.760
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.400
Closing, Tommy. You're wonderful. Thank you.

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:20.130
Ride, kids. Rehearsal at 10 o'clock tomorrow morning.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:21.830
Half of you dance like you were flat-footed.

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:23.130
Now, go on. Get out of here, all of you.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:25.730
It's lack of food.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.460
Food? Artists don't think of food.

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:29.970
I hate...

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.500
We need to be sorted, Mr. Frost.

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:33.860
But we've all been on rehearsal pages.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:37.460
Have you no faith?

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:39.060
Oh, sure, I have faith.

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:40.650
Not much hope.

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:42.850
Mr. Frost, could I speak to you?

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:43.990
Tomorrow, dear, tomorrow.

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:44.710
Charlie?

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:46.090
Yes, Mr. Frost?

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:47.890
Stop them from loading that scenery.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:48.430
Get it back.

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:49.250
Yes, sir.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:50.730
You're loaded.

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:53.030
Aye, we are.

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:53.550
Good.

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:55.150
Mr. Jonesville says take it back in again.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:57.750
And none of your outbursts of charm.

00:03:57.910 --> 00:03:58.330
I'm through.

00:03:58.490 --> 00:03:59.370
But, Phyllis, please.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:03:59.970
No money.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.280
No evening date, no system, nothing but care.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:04.400
Honey, calm me.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:05.780
Oh, you can find another star.

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:07.020
But, fellas, you're going too far.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.700
On the contrary, I haven't gone far enough.

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:11.370
No, wait a minute.

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:48.910
Oh, hello, Mrs. Urquhart. Feet hurt?

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:52.470
Oh, no. We just didn't want to wake everybody up.

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:54.230
That's very considerate of you.

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:55.690
And while you're being considerate,

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:57.730
there's just a little matter of two weeks' rent.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:59.380
Oh, we'll pay you, Mrs. Urquhart.

00:04:59.440 --> 00:04:59.960
Haven't you any...

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.540
Now, listen, you two, I was in show business before you were born.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:05.680
I've crept up more than you'll ever creep up.

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:08.710
But this is stretching Anglo-American relations too far.

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:12.510
Look, here are a couple of tickets. They're for opening night.

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:15.170
Thanks. You've already given me half the first row.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:19.370
Mrs. Urquhart, we appealed your loyalty to Edinburgh.

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:22.230
All right, you win. Go on up.

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:26.500
Oh, I forgot. You've got a visitor sitting outside your door.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:27.740
Visitor? A visitor?

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:29.980
A woman from the dressmaker. She's after her.

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:31.320
Come with me.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:38.540
My old man used to sneak in this way after a night with the boys.

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:43.060
All I can say is Mr. Urquhart is a very lucky man.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:45.220
He is. He's been dead 10 years.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:46.660
Now, quick, out the fire, babe.

00:05:59.510 --> 00:05:59.970
We'll be late.

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:06.480
Me! Me! Get up!

00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:09.450
Look at the time.

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:37.000
Immediately, in my skirt.

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:38.380
Lipism!

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:43.440
My bag, my gloves, and the drawer.

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:48.320
You've got to hurry, too, quickly.

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:53.960
I'm entitled to noise.

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:54.800
Ten pass worth.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:55.740
Where's Miss Jones?

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:56.840
She left for the theater.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:57.980
Didn't you see her go?

00:06:58.200 --> 00:06:59.380
Did you tell me that?

00:06:59.700 --> 00:06:59.980
She's.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:00.860
Here, I know it.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:02.620
Why don't you look under the bed?

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:03.760
Please, my lassie.

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:05.540
I was told no to come back without the money.

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:06.540
She's not here.

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:08.500
I've told you she's gone to the theater.

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.540
We've got a rehearsal at 9.30.

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:11.920
I'm very late myself.

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:24.440
Did you signal me?

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:25.460
Yes, I did.

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:26.480
I hope you don't mind.

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:27.580
Only I'm awfully late.

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:28.040
Not a bit.

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:28.600
Get in.

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:31.810
American, aren't you?

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:32.880
Why, yes.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:33.620
How did you know?

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:35.240
You use this so gracefully.

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:43.310
It's very nice of you, Mr.

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:44.810
Bates is the name.

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:46.310
I'm Janet Jones.

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:48.180
You say you work at the Mercury Theater?

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:50.880
Not if we don't get there in 15 minutes.

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:52.080
We'll do it in 10.

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:01.970
This would have to happen.

00:08:07.030 --> 00:08:08.870
I'll never get to the theater on time.

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:10.740
Can't we go around him?

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:12.760
We shouldn't, but I will.

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:24.960
Dear, think the police are following us.

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:25.380
Really?

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:28.860
Maybe I was wrong about that 10 minutes.

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:44.560
I told you yesterday, this show's going to open with or without money and with or without a star.

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:45.560
Now get the rehearsal going.

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:29.940
I told you to finish facing up there.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:30.840
You did?

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:32.420
Me? Never.

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:34.520
It's no use appealing to the cheap seats.

00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:37.030
Go on your knees to the expensive ones like this

00:09:37.030 --> 00:09:39.720
and play it down there. That's where the dough comes from.

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:41.610
All right, let's try it once more.

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:42.550
Okay, hit it.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:07.180
Now, Charlie, you're not going to tell on me.

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:08.940
Now, listen, my duty as a stage manager to see that you...

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:10.480
And the best stage manager in the business...

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:11.980
My duty as a stage manager is...

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:14.520
He is to see that Mr. Frost doesn't have any more worries

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:16.440
than he's got already, and you're doing it wonderfully.

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:18.290
You're a sweet little man.

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:52.390
I'm sorry, Mr. Frost. I thought you said it this way.

00:10:52.570 --> 00:10:53.530
That was yesterday.

00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:55.250
She didn't know you'd changed it.

00:10:55.290 --> 00:10:56.890
Of course she didn't. And shut up!

00:10:57.480 --> 00:10:58.740
You just came in. I saw you.

00:11:00.520 --> 00:11:01.900
Yes, you certainly did.

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:04.700
You ended up this way instead of this way.

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:05.580
I'm sorry.

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:07.000
I'm sorry for you.

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:09.930
You spend your life being just a halfway good chorus girl.

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:11.460
And that goes for all of you.

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:13.990
How do you suppose I got to the position I'm in today?

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:15.340
Well, I'll tell you.

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:20.320
Through grit, determination, and punctuality.

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:23.940
It's just that our alarm clock didn't go off this morning.

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:26.420
Alarm clock. Stars aren't made by alarm clocks.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:27.700
Stars are made by talent.

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:29.460
That's why you'll never get out of the chorus.

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:32.730
That's where you're wrong, Mr. Pross, because I am out.

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:33.480
I quit.

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:40.110
I want to see Miss Janet Jones, please.

00:11:40.390 --> 00:11:40.910
I'm sorry.

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:41.830
You'll have to wait.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:44.640
May I see Miss Janet Jones, please?

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:45.300
Not now.

00:11:45.420 --> 00:11:46.220
She's rehearsing.

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:47.940
You just take your turn.

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:49.940
I have a prior claimant, Miss Jones.

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:51.300
I only want to return her bag.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:52.400
She left it in the car.

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:55.380
No one sees anyone until the rehearsal is over.

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:56.540
Any calls for me, Mac?

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:57.280
No, my dear.

00:11:57.460 --> 00:11:57.700
No.

00:11:59.190 --> 00:11:59.590
Oh.

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:02.130
Are you Mr. Drummond's chauffeur?

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:03.210
No, I'm Mr. Bruno's.

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:05.950
Not Mr. BG Bruno, the greeting card manufacturer.

00:12:06.110 --> 00:12:06.690
The very same.

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:09.210
Oh, he didn't send you here for me, did he?

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:10.210
Betty Summers?

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:11.010
I'm afraid not.

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:12.290
I'm waiting for Miss Jones.

00:12:12.660 --> 00:12:13.420
Janet Jones?

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:14.360
Are you a friend of hers?

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:15.360
Yes.

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:17.140
Well, will you do me a favor, miss?

00:12:17.350 --> 00:12:18.170
Give her this bag.

00:12:18.310 --> 00:12:19.230
She left it in the car.

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:20.030
Why, of course.

00:12:20.620 --> 00:12:22.700
And give my love to Mr. Bruno.

00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:24.820
Somehow, I don't think he'd appreciate it.

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:31.370
Janice Jones.

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:33.090
Well, well.

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:36.930
I don't think I'll wait after all.

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:39.450
Please don't bother to tell Miss Jones I was here.

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:44.170
Oh, sorry, Mr. Frost, I didn't see you.

00:12:44.310 --> 00:12:46.210
If you put as much energy into your dancing

00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:48.190
as you do into running blindfold down passages,

00:12:48.270 --> 00:12:49.170
we might have a show.

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:50.250
Yes, Mr. Frost.

00:12:51.820 --> 00:12:52.560
What have you got there?

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:54.560
A bag, Janet Jones's bag.

00:12:54.990 --> 00:12:56.570
She's B.G. Bruno's girlfriend.

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:58.010
So is that any reason to go to?

00:12:59.360 --> 00:12:59.900
She's whose?

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:01.130
B.G. Bruno.

00:13:01.770 --> 00:13:03.670
B.G. Bruno's one of the richest men in Scotland.

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:04.470
That's right.

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:05.350
He's a millionaire.

00:13:05.570 --> 00:13:06.550
He's five millionaires.

00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:07.270
I looked him up.

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:10.730
So he's going around with one of our girls, huh?

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:13.340
Well, what do you know?

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:15.570
What's your name?

00:13:15.750 --> 00:13:16.450
Betty Summers.

00:13:16.590 --> 00:13:18.290
I'm the girl that's been wanting to talk to you about it.

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:18.450
Oh, not now.

00:13:18.510 --> 00:13:19.370
Not now, Betsy.

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:19.990
Betty!

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:20.550
Yeah, yes.

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:22.030
Well, I'll see that Janet Jones gets the back.

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:22.470
Oh, yes, sir.

00:13:22.490 --> 00:13:24.230
But if you could just give me a few minutes, then I can...

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:25.510
I'll give you much more than that.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:27.630
I'll give you a raise next time I pay you.

00:13:27.810 --> 00:13:27.930
Oh.

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:28.920
Charlie!

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:29.980
Yes, Betty?

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.030
Mr. Frost, don't do that.

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:33.570
Oh, I gotta talk to you.

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:35.050
Who does he think he is?

00:13:35.690 --> 00:13:37.710
Telling me I'd never get out of the chorus.

00:13:37.990 --> 00:13:40.190
Listen, you'll never get out of town

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:41.510
if you don't earn some money.

00:13:42.390 --> 00:13:44.070
You're going straight up to Frosty

00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:45.350
and play the prodigal daughter.

00:13:45.890 --> 00:13:46.850
I am not.

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:49.220
After those insults.

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:50.310
Why should I?

00:13:51.110 --> 00:13:51.930
Several reasons.

00:13:52.940 --> 00:13:55.060
One dress bill, two weeks rent in a row.

00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:55.800
Shall I go on?

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:57.900
Can't be that dumb.

00:13:58.470 --> 00:13:59.970
Janet Jones, one of our girls, is...

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.000
is going with BG Bruno.

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:02.700
BG Bruno, the millionaire?

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:05.980
Multi, Charlie, multi.

00:14:06.260 --> 00:14:07.820
He's worth five million, maybe six.

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:11.910
Janet Jones, the millionaire.

00:14:13.550 --> 00:14:14.470
What a pity.

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:15.640
Why a pity?

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:17.500
She's a wonderful girl, the greatest.

00:14:17.780 --> 00:14:18.580
Go and get her, quick.

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:21.390
Janet isn't with the show anymore.

00:14:21.550 --> 00:14:22.230
Don't argue.

00:14:22.390 --> 00:14:22.910
We're saved.

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:26.410
If BG Bruno loves her, what do you

00:14:26.410 --> 00:14:27.370
mean she's not in the show anymore?

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:27.990
Well, don't you remember?

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:28.870
She quit at rehearsal.

00:14:30.280 --> 00:14:32.200
Oh, so that's the little...

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:34.230
We'll start her. That's what we'll do.

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:35.150
Where does she live?

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:35.850
I don't know.

00:14:36.070 --> 00:14:37.390
Well, why don't you know?

00:14:38.130 --> 00:14:39.940
Am I asking the impossible?

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:46.420
A well-run office, they'd find it like that.

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:48.990
Trouble is, there's no system around here, no initiative.

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:51.180
Do I have to teach her how to file, too?

00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:54.200
Oh, excuse me, Mr. Frost.

00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:56.420
Not now, later. Can't you see I'm busy?

00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:57.760
Don't we have a list of the cast?

00:14:57.840 --> 00:14:58.640
Don't we know where they live?

00:14:58.840 --> 00:14:59.980
Suppose somebody got sick, what...

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:00.420
What would you do?

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:01.160
Call a doctor.

00:15:01.220 --> 00:15:02.580
Oh, call a doctor.

00:15:02.780 --> 00:15:04.100
I only wanted to work.

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:05.200
Here, you might as well help, too.

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:05.880
Look through these.

00:15:06.020 --> 00:15:08.920
Who are you?

00:15:10.540 --> 00:15:11.280
Janet Jones.

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:13.000
Well, don't stand there making idle talk.

00:15:13.080 --> 00:15:13.780
Look for the address.

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:16.580
Whose address are we looking for?

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:18.340
Janet Jones!

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:24.470
Who did you say you were?

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:26.620
Janet Jones.

00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:27.780
Oh.

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:28.880
Charlie!

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:31.240
Janet Jones.

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:33.440
You see, I have to do everything.

00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:35.900
Well, Miss Jones, where have you been?

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:37.240
We've been looking all over for you.

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:38.200
Come in, please.

00:15:39.150 --> 00:15:39.890
Right this way.

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:42.090
I'm sorry you walked in on such a mess,

00:15:42.110 --> 00:15:43.050
but we were trying to find it.

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:45.030
Mr. Frost, I came here to apologize

00:15:45.030 --> 00:15:46.530
for my behavior on the stage.

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.500
I guess I lost my temper.

00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:49.560
And why shouldn't you?

00:15:50.450 --> 00:15:52.610
If there's one thing I like, it's a girl with spirit.

00:15:52.960 --> 00:15:54.020
Oh, here's your bag.

00:15:55.520 --> 00:15:56.300
But where did you?

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:57.740
No, it's no time to discuss that.

00:15:57.860 --> 00:15:59.140
We've got to discuss you and the show.

00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:01.400
Well, get me a standard contract.

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:03.910
I really can dance, you know.

00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:06.470
I don't think you've ever seen me do a real solo.

00:16:06.510 --> 00:16:07.890
Well, I don't have to, darling.

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:08.830
I don't have to.

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:11.980
I suppose now you can't even find a simple contract.

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:13.510
Look, Mr. Frost.

00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:17.960
It's a piece of paper this size.

00:16:17.960 --> 00:16:19.220
A baby could find it.

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:22.470
Yeah, that's wonderful, honey.

00:16:22.550 --> 00:16:23.910
We'll work out some great routines.

00:16:24.570 --> 00:16:25.950
I could do acrobatic, too.

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:32.900
No, Mr. Frost, I can't...

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:34.420
There, you see how simple it is?

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:42.100
Oh, no! Are you hurt?

00:16:43.040 --> 00:16:45.900
No. Oh, thank heavens. Here, sign this.

00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:49.170
I can sing, too. Yeah, yeah, yeah, sign it.

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:02.010
You're going to star me in the show?

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:02.390
No!

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:13.550
Jones, I do hope you don't mind us coming in.

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:14.910
Ah, it is Miss Jones.

00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:17.240
Bonjour, mademoiselle.

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:19.440
Now, madame Amanda, I've already told you

00:17:19.440 --> 00:17:20.800
why I can't pay you until Friday.

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:21.260
Pay?

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:23.400
Oh, mademoiselle, you s'en prie,

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:25.400
do not mention such a thing.

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:27.220
Regardez tout ce que je vous ai apparté

00:17:27.220 --> 00:17:29.140
for you to try on.

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:36.450
Yes, Miss Penfold, the first we call blue moonlight.

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:37.470
Claire de lune.

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:38.890
Isn't it wonderful?

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:39.900
Beautiful.

00:17:40.460 --> 00:17:41.420
We will try it on.

00:17:41.720 --> 00:17:42.560
Et vous verrez, n'est-ce pas?

00:17:43.020 --> 00:17:44.060
Oh, c'est une robe délicieuse.

00:17:45.400 --> 00:17:47.300
And Mademoiselle has just the figure.

00:17:47.860 --> 00:17:48.580
What's the waste?

00:17:48.820 --> 00:17:49.580
Step out, please.

00:17:49.800 --> 00:17:51.160
Don't you think she has, Miss Penfold?

00:17:51.180 --> 00:17:52.200
Oh, yes, madame.

00:17:52.320 --> 00:17:52.800
Of course.

00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:53.760
There are others.

00:17:53.980 --> 00:17:55.400
But you can try them out at your leisure.

00:17:55.960 --> 00:17:57.020
Step in, please.

00:17:57.680 --> 00:17:58.580
Miss Penfold.

00:17:58.860 --> 00:17:59.600
Yes, madame.

00:17:59.600 --> 00:17:59.980
you have no

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:04.280
forgotten to bring the silver suit, the rouge chiffon, and Le Coquelicot.

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:07.800
Maintenant. Oh, mon dieu, you have not got anywhere.

00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:12.450
From here, from the west, up.

00:18:12.920 --> 00:18:14.920
Now, what do you think of that?

00:18:16.460 --> 00:18:17.390
Perfect, beautiful.

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:18.740
Oh, Miss Benvolte.

00:18:20.110 --> 00:18:23.920
Yes, see? What? You don't understand.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:27.260
Voila! With the compliment of Madame Amanda.

00:18:27.560 --> 00:18:28.560
It is Hermine.

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:29.800
Madame Amanda?

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:34.670
You could have the silver mink, too, Miss Penfold.

00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:38.640
You are brilliant, but of course,

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:42.630
a mademoiselle can have the silver mink, too, voila.

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:48.520
Not a word.

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:51.930
Excuse that you look at the other trifles.

00:18:52.600 --> 00:18:55.250
Madame Amanda, did Mr. Frost tell me?

00:18:55.250 --> 00:18:56.210
Oh, ne vous jenez pas.

00:18:56.670 --> 00:18:58.550
Let us not worry who tell me anything.

00:18:58.790 --> 00:18:59.970
It is a little...

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:01.000
C'est secret, n'est-ce pas?

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:03.260
C'est l'amour.

00:19:04.180 --> 00:19:06.510
Maintenant, venez donc, Miss Penfold.

00:19:07.090 --> 00:19:08.510
Mademoiselle must be tired.

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:10.630
And if there is anything else you want,

00:19:10.930 --> 00:19:12.530
un coup de téléphone tout simplement.

00:19:12.850 --> 00:19:14.330
Promise you will telephone me.

00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:15.340
I promise.

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:17.600
Merci bien, mademoiselle. Au revoir.

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:19.730
Chantez comme Miss Penfold.

00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:32.350
Lady, isn't it?

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:34.370
Must be.

00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:46.240
But May, Dad.

00:19:46.240 --> 00:19:47.640
Oh, May, am I glad to see you.

00:19:47.880 --> 00:19:49.160
Now take a deep breath and listen.

00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:51.380
I'm listening, but I got no breath.

00:19:51.740 --> 00:19:53.060
Frosty's given me a contract,

00:19:53.430 --> 00:19:55.550
and Madame Amanda gave me all this.

00:19:55.650 --> 00:19:57.790
And where are you stabling your race horses?

00:19:58.070 --> 00:19:59.930
May, please, you've got to be serious.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.010
a soddy in Edinburgh has got to keep their sanity.

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:03.400
What does all this mean?

00:20:03.660 --> 00:20:04.440
You don't know.

00:20:04.660 --> 00:20:05.860
Well, of course I don't.

00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:08.620
Janet Jones, I think you're a stinker.

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:11.520
Oh, May, don't you start acting crazy too.

00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:14.980
Well, while you cool off, I'll slip...

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:17.560
I would too if I were you.

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:20.400
I don't know what you're so huffy about.

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:22.860
Well, you could at least tell your best friend.

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:25.880
But I'm trying to tell you if you'll listen a minute.

00:20:26.080 --> 00:20:29.460
You're mad.

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:32.730
I suppose everybody at the theater's mad, too.

00:20:32.950 --> 00:20:37.240
I suppose you think it's nice for me, your best friend, to be the last to hear the news.

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:39.810
What news? I don't know what you're talking about.

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:42.540
Do you mean you're still going to deny it?

00:20:42.660 --> 00:20:44.190
Of course I deny it.

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:48.900
I repeat, Janet Jones, I think you're a stinker.

00:20:48.980 --> 00:20:53.240
The whole world's gone mad.

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:56.040
Why do you think Frost is starring you in the show?

00:20:56.140 --> 00:20:57.700
And Old Amanda gave you this lot?

00:20:57.740 --> 00:20:57.960
Why?

00:20:58.300 --> 00:20:59.240
Well, why?

00:21:00.028 --> 00:21:01.028
E.G. Bruno.

00:21:02.044 --> 00:21:04.784
Look, will you please tell me who is this B.G. Bruno?

00:21:05.628 --> 00:21:09.128
He happens to have made millions out of greeting cards.

00:21:09.212 --> 00:21:12.512
Furthermore, he happens to be the richest man in Scotland.

00:21:12.732 --> 00:21:14.212
He still doesn't mean a thing to me.

00:21:14.684 --> 00:21:16.184
He doesn't mean a thing to her.

00:21:16.412 --> 00:21:18.212
Listen to me, Janet Jones.

00:21:18.240 --> 00:21:22.320
Will you take an oath on all you hold dear that you aren't engaged to BG Bruno?

00:21:23.068 --> 00:21:25.028
Engaged to him? I don't even know him.

00:21:33.070 --> 00:21:38.490
Will you please tell me what you're laughing at?

00:21:39.920 --> 00:21:41.640
Don't you think it's funny?

00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:46.060
You get dressed and starred on account of a man you don't even know.

00:21:46.620 --> 00:21:50.300
I think it's horrible.

00:21:51.670 --> 00:21:54.570
Listen, Frosty thinks he's pulling a fast one.

00:21:55.090 --> 00:21:57.650
Star the girl and the fiancé will put money in the show.

00:21:58.340 --> 00:21:59.800
You don't honestly think... Why not?

00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:00.990
It's been done before.

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:04.010
Want me to name a few stars who started that way?

00:22:04.640 --> 00:22:05.020
No.

00:22:09.110 --> 00:22:09.570
Come in.

00:22:10.850 --> 00:22:11.530
Miss Jones?

00:22:12.300 --> 00:22:12.660
Yes?

00:22:14.410 --> 00:22:15.450
Will you sign here, please?

00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:22.990
Blow me down from Frosty.

00:22:24.540 --> 00:22:25.920
Then you can take them right back.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:32.640
Uh, just a minute, I'll take it.

00:22:41.560 --> 00:22:44.460
If you said your prayers for a break, well, you've got it.

00:22:44.900 --> 00:22:46.180
I don't want a break this way.

00:22:46.260 --> 00:22:47.860
Oh, what difference which way?

00:22:48.120 --> 00:22:50.500
If you make the grades, you can always tell them afterwards.

00:22:50.870 --> 00:22:54.010
You didn't tell Frosty you were engaged to old moneybags, did you?

00:22:54.440 --> 00:22:54.960
No, but I still...

00:22:54.960 --> 00:22:57.820
And you didn't tell old Madam Guillotine you had money, did you?

00:22:58.680 --> 00:22:59.040
No.

00:23:01.690 --> 00:23:01.950
Uh-huh.

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:36.490
Mr. Bruno.

00:23:40.940 --> 00:23:41.440
Mr. Bruno.

00:23:58.540 --> 00:23:58.660
Bruno.

00:24:05.852 --> 00:24:06.592
Mr. Bruno.

00:24:31.468 --> 00:24:31.968
Well...

00:24:32.780 --> 00:24:33.820
It's a mistake.

00:24:33.820 --> 00:24:36.080
But it does say BG Bruno.

00:24:36.080 --> 00:24:38.500
Whatever it says, you know and I know.

00:24:38.500 --> 00:24:39.500
It's a mistake.

00:24:50.604 --> 00:24:52.604
This young woman had actually visited you here.

00:24:53.068 --> 00:24:54.108
During office hours.

00:24:54.380 --> 00:24:55.880
In the Easter Room...

00:24:56.108 --> 00:24:58.068
Well, quite frankly, Harold, I was flabbergasted.

00:24:58.540 --> 00:24:59.620
I don't want this to happen again.

00:25:01.370 --> 00:25:02.570
No, yes, Mr. Bruno.

00:25:02.770 --> 00:25:05.420
We have a staff outing once a year for that sort of thing.

00:25:05.840 --> 00:25:06.640
Yes, Mr. Bruno.

00:25:07.200 --> 00:25:09.840
Harold, I have no wish to pry into other people's private lives.

00:25:10.000 --> 00:25:12.910
But here in Bruno House, I will not have the members of my...

00:25:15.990 --> 00:25:16.330
What is this?

00:25:16.710 --> 00:25:19.050
It seems to be some sort of a bill, sir.

00:25:19.270 --> 00:25:23.970
I will not have the members of my staff mixing business with pleasure.

00:25:24.130 --> 00:25:26.110
There are certain standards of decorum...

00:25:32.750 --> 00:25:34.390
A decorum which I insist upon being observed.

00:25:35.120 --> 00:25:35.740
You may go, Harold.

00:25:36.240 --> 00:25:37.060
Yes, Mr. Brunner.

00:25:37.180 --> 00:25:41.160
Now, what is all this about?

00:25:42.980 --> 00:25:44.020
Amanda, Princeton Street.

00:25:44.120 --> 00:25:44.900
Why is this addressed to me?

00:25:45.000 --> 00:25:46.400
Well, that's what I was wondering, sir.

00:25:46.680 --> 00:25:48.180
Miss Janet Jones, Mercury Theatre.

00:25:48.360 --> 00:25:51.880
Silver mink stole, ermine wrapped, sat in negligee.

00:25:52.020 --> 00:25:54.100
Well, this is monstrous, preposterous.

00:25:54.200 --> 00:25:55.680
I'd never been near the Mercury Theatre.

00:25:55.740 --> 00:25:56.740
I'd never heard of Janet Jones.

00:25:56.880 --> 00:25:57.620
You deal with this.

00:26:00.444 --> 00:26:01.584
What are you looking at me like that for?

00:26:02.140 --> 00:26:02.900
Like what, sir?

00:26:04.508 --> 00:26:06.608
You surely don't think that I have anything to do with this.

00:26:06.668 --> 00:26:07.428
You, Mr. Bruno?

00:26:07.808 --> 00:26:09.048
Why, of course not, sir.

00:26:09.468 --> 00:26:10.208
Of course not.

00:26:10.844 --> 00:26:12.784
I knew there must have been some mistake.

00:26:14.012 --> 00:26:15.012
Well, I must have been.

00:26:15.012 --> 00:26:17.012
Well, sir, I knew that you couldn't.

00:26:17.372 --> 00:26:18.272
What do you mean, I couldn't?

00:26:18.620 --> 00:26:20.320
Well, sir, I mean that you wouldn't.

00:26:20.892 --> 00:26:22.392
Well, I should hope not, Mr. Dawson.

00:26:23.676 --> 00:26:25.676
Answer the telephone.

00:26:27.836 --> 00:26:28.796
Mr. Bruno's office.

00:26:30.920 --> 00:26:31.220
The what?

00:26:31.440 --> 00:26:36.040
The Mercury Theatre, sir.

00:26:36.160 --> 00:26:37.070
For you.

00:26:37.310 --> 00:26:37.590
Hello?

00:26:41.230 --> 00:26:43.190
I have wonderful news for you, Mr. Bruno.

00:26:43.430 --> 00:26:44.520
Yes, for you.

00:26:45.540 --> 00:26:47.020
We're going to star Miss Janet Jones.

00:26:47.360 --> 00:26:49.520
This is BG Bruno Limited. There's some mistake.

00:26:49.860 --> 00:26:52.680
Oh, no, there's no mistake. I've had my eye on her for some time.

00:26:52.860 --> 00:26:54.530
We're going to build a show around her.

00:26:56.570 --> 00:26:58.210
Look, is this a practical joke or something?

00:26:58.290 --> 00:26:59.830
I tell you, I've never heard of Janet Jones.

00:27:00.500 --> 00:27:03.050
I quite understand, Mr. Bruno.

00:27:03.850 --> 00:27:05.960
Well, now do you believe me?

00:27:06.060 --> 00:27:13.240
Yes. There you go again.

00:27:14.340 --> 00:27:14.760
What, sir?

00:27:14.860 --> 00:27:16.780
Looking at me in that surreptitious way.

00:27:16.920 --> 00:27:17.980
Tell you I've never heard of this girl.

00:27:18.100 --> 00:27:19.650
Of course not, Mr. Bruno.

00:27:19.930 --> 00:27:23.270
The whole thing's a practical joke, or something worse.

00:27:26.960 --> 00:27:29.970
If I were you, sir, I should get in touch with the police.

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:31.860
And have the firm involved in the scandal?

00:27:32.040 --> 00:27:35.260
Oh, no. I shall deal with this in my own way.

00:27:37.600 --> 00:27:40.180
Was I looking that way again, sir?

00:27:40.340 --> 00:27:41.040
You were.

00:27:41.260 --> 00:27:44.970
It was unintentional, I assure you.

00:27:45.900 --> 00:27:48.460
I should hope so, Mr. Dodds.

00:27:48.520 --> 00:27:51.190
Now, we're going to do the number again,

00:27:51.230 --> 00:27:53.730
and this time we're going to do it from the beginning right through to the finish.

00:27:54.410 --> 00:27:55.350
Everybody take the positions.

00:28:32.200 --> 00:28:32.420
Thank you very much.

00:30:31.370 --> 00:30:33.210
That was fine, Janet. You're wonderful.

00:30:33.530 --> 00:30:35.130
There are one or two things we can polish up later.

00:30:35.500 --> 00:30:36.380
Thank you, Mr. Frost.

00:30:36.660 --> 00:30:39.920
I'm still having little trouble with the downstage spins, but I'll get them.

00:30:40.020 --> 00:30:41.060
You bet you'll get them.

00:30:41.300 --> 00:30:42.660
Now go and have that new costume fitted.

00:30:45.880 --> 00:30:47.750
Mac, appointment with Janet Jones.

00:30:48.080 --> 00:30:50.100
That's right, Mr. Tracy. She's expecting you.

00:30:50.300 --> 00:30:50.760
Go on in.

00:30:51.040 --> 00:30:51.360
Okay.

00:30:52.150 --> 00:30:55.600
Now, Mr. Tracy, it should make a grand story for you, eh?

00:30:56.070 --> 00:30:59.110
From chorus girl to star in one jump.

00:30:59.270 --> 00:30:59.670
Aye.

00:31:00.060 --> 00:31:00.820
I hope you're right.

00:31:09.590 --> 00:31:10.910
Paul Tracy, Morning Express.

00:31:11.360 --> 00:31:11.940
Oh, hello.

00:31:12.300 --> 00:31:13.280
Would you mind waiting a minute?

00:31:13.930 --> 00:31:14.870
Sure, that's OK.

00:31:15.900 --> 00:31:16.400
No hurry.

00:31:24.480 --> 00:31:26.340
Tracy, my boy, how nice to see you.

00:31:26.460 --> 00:31:27.160
Come and have a drink.

00:31:27.320 --> 00:31:29.000
I will after, but Miss Jones here.

00:31:29.020 --> 00:31:29.980
Oh, you've got a minute, Chief.

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:31.480
She just went in to change her costume anyway.

00:31:31.680 --> 00:31:32.080
Come on.

00:31:36.690 --> 00:31:37.050
Yes, sir.

00:31:38.310 --> 00:31:39.590
I want to speak to Miss Janet Jones.

00:31:39.770 --> 00:31:41.230
I'm afraid she's busy at the moment.

00:31:41.620 --> 00:31:42.080
What name?

00:31:42.320 --> 00:31:42.900
Mr. Bruno.

00:31:44.360 --> 00:31:45.580
B.G. Bruno.

00:31:46.180 --> 00:31:46.840
That is correct.

00:31:47.260 --> 00:31:48.220
Oh, certainly, sir.

00:31:48.600 --> 00:31:50.000
Please walk right in, Mr. Bruno.

00:31:50.140 --> 00:31:52.360
Through the swing door, first passage on the right,

00:31:52.700 --> 00:31:53.620
room number one.

00:31:53.850 --> 00:31:54.210
Thank you.

00:31:56.260 --> 00:31:56.880
Thank you, sir.

00:32:08.250 --> 00:32:10.140
All right, you may come in now.

00:32:14.960 --> 00:32:16.660
That's fine, Maggie. I'll send it up to you later.

00:32:16.780 --> 00:32:19.790
It's all fixed. Mind the pins when you take it off.

00:32:19.970 --> 00:32:20.470
Yes, Maggie.

00:32:22.190 --> 00:32:24.530
I'm sorry you caught me like this. How do you do?

00:32:25.540 --> 00:32:26.060
How do you do?

00:32:26.370 --> 00:32:27.810
I didn't mean to keep you waiting.

00:32:28.620 --> 00:32:29.240
Won't you sit down?

00:32:29.500 --> 00:32:29.880
Miss Jones.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:32.800
I have come here to get to the bottom of a certain matter.

00:32:33.650 --> 00:32:34.010
Yes?

00:32:34.400 --> 00:32:37.320
Which, to put it frankly, and not to beat about the...

00:32:37.660 --> 00:32:38.480
You Janet Jones?

00:32:39.640 --> 00:32:41.180
Why, yes. Am I a disappointment?

00:32:41.590 --> 00:32:44.870
Oh, no. No, I just expected something rather different, that's all.

00:32:45.550 --> 00:32:47.420
Oh, I see. Please sit down.

00:32:47.580 --> 00:32:49.440
And you won't mind if I change this, will you?

00:32:49.540 --> 00:32:52.530
Oh, no. Oh, no! Well, look, I'll wait outside, shall I...

00:32:52.530 --> 00:32:53.610
Oh, no, I can talk from behind here.

00:32:54.500 --> 00:32:56.800
You know, I thought you'd be quite different, too.

00:32:57.060 --> 00:32:59.140
Me? You mean you were expecting me?

00:33:00.570 --> 00:33:17.140
of course then you know what i've come about naturally why did you do it well i always wanted

00:33:17.140 --> 00:33:24.160
to ever since i was a child my father was dead against it i should hope so too on the other

00:33:24.160 --> 00:33:29.620
hand my mother encouraged me your mother encouraged you to practice a deception

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:31.000
Well, there was no deception.

00:33:31.440 --> 00:33:34.670
I merely said I wanted to go on the stage, and I went.

00:33:35.500 --> 00:33:39.670
Miss Jones, that is not the explanation I require.

00:33:40.180 --> 00:33:41.740
Oh, I know you want something more colorful.

00:33:42.950 --> 00:33:44.330
You know, I can't get over you.

00:33:44.620 --> 00:33:47.040
When they told me Paul Tracy was coming to interview me,

00:33:47.420 --> 00:33:50.420
I expected some hard, fast-talking, moving newspaper man.

00:33:51.110 --> 00:33:52.090
But you're not.

00:33:52.250 --> 00:33:54.470
Miss Jones, this name of Paul Tracy.

00:33:54.670 --> 00:33:56.610
Oh, it's probably not your real name at all.

00:33:57.610 --> 00:33:59.970
Anyway, I find you most comfortable to talk to.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:01.840
Oh, you do?

00:34:03.560 --> 00:34:06.740
Well, as a matter of fact, I don't find you as uncomfortable as I expected either.

00:34:08.840 --> 00:34:10.380
Oh, you're very... you've got a lawyer.

00:34:11.600 --> 00:34:13.420
What a charming room this is.

00:34:14.570 --> 00:34:15.750
Thank you. I'm glad you like it.

00:34:16.480 --> 00:34:17.960
I've only been in here since this morning,

00:34:18.310 --> 00:34:21.130
but gay drapes and flowers always help, don't they?

00:34:21.960 --> 00:34:22.380
Do they?

00:34:23.150 --> 00:34:23.790
Why, certainly.

00:34:26.660 --> 00:34:28.480
Shall I begin at the beginning?

00:34:28.940 --> 00:34:29.820
Yes, please do.

00:34:30.540 --> 00:34:31.260
Well, let's sit down.

00:34:33.920 --> 00:34:35.620
Would you like to know where I was born?

00:34:37.090 --> 00:34:38.410
Yes, I'd love to.

00:34:39.080 --> 00:34:41.620
Well, I was born on a little farm in Virginia.

00:34:42.190 --> 00:34:43.510
That's amazing. So was I.

00:34:44.520 --> 00:34:44.800
What?

00:34:45.260 --> 00:34:47.300
Oh, not on the same farm. No, ours was Devonshire.

00:34:47.860 --> 00:34:48.960
Then I went to school at Harrow.

00:34:49.160 --> 00:34:51.260
I left when I was 16, because I couldn't stand it any longer.

00:34:51.500 --> 00:34:54.470
But my father had very definite ideas about how life should be lived.

00:34:54.610 --> 00:34:55.250
And he said...

00:34:55.250 --> 00:34:57.500
Oh, pardon me, but who is interviewing whom?

00:34:58.220 --> 00:34:59.500
Oh, I'm sorry, I forgot.

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:03.180
Well, it was a little rose-covered cottage

00:35:03.910 --> 00:35:07.430
nestled among the magnolia trees, down near a lake.

00:35:08.340 --> 00:35:11.150
And every morning, I used to get up very early

00:35:11.150 --> 00:35:13.040
and milk all the cows.

00:35:13.690 --> 00:35:14.450
How many cows?

00:35:15.100 --> 00:35:19.510
Fifty. What are you smiling at?

00:35:19.710 --> 00:35:20.910
Oh, nothing. Please go on.

00:35:21.850 --> 00:35:22.890
You don't believe me?

00:35:23.180 --> 00:35:25.620
Oh, it's just that I know about farms. I've got some.

00:35:26.470 --> 00:35:27.070
You have?

00:35:28.300 --> 00:35:29.960
I mean, I've got some relatives and things that...

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:31.800
I live on farms and I know what they are.

00:35:33.250 --> 00:35:33.730
Oh, you do?

00:35:35.760 --> 00:35:36.360
All right.

00:35:36.620 --> 00:35:38.900
It was a plain brick house with no roses,

00:35:39.480 --> 00:35:42.300
not a tree or a cow for miles.

00:35:42.440 --> 00:35:43.380
It wasn't in Virginia.

00:35:44.250 --> 00:35:45.270
Hoboken, New Jersey.

00:35:46.250 --> 00:35:49.990
She was born on a tuna fishing boat off the coast of Mexico.

00:35:50.590 --> 00:35:52.090
Her mother was a former Ziegfeld girl.

00:35:52.360 --> 00:35:54.060
She met Jana's father and gave up a career.

00:35:54.240 --> 00:35:55.100
She loved him that much.

00:35:55.430 --> 00:35:57.310
He was a deep sea diver on the side.

00:35:57.410 --> 00:35:59.490
How much is Bruno putting into the show?

00:36:00.220 --> 00:36:01.460
Now, get this for real drama.

00:36:02.080 --> 00:36:03.420
Her mother taught her everything she knew.

00:36:03.790 --> 00:36:06.170
And when a storm wrecked the boat and they didn't have a dime,

00:36:06.880 --> 00:36:07.980
what do you think the poor kid did?

00:36:09.570 --> 00:36:11.010
Went off and met B.G. Bruno.

00:36:12.470 --> 00:36:13.610
Why don't you give him a drink?

00:36:15.360 --> 00:36:17.480
Then bingo. Out of the blue, I got this break.

00:36:17.720 --> 00:36:19.290
Wonderful. How did you get it?

00:36:20.520 --> 00:36:21.400
Well, I...

00:36:21.840 --> 00:36:24.160
Was it hard work or influence or what?

00:36:25.680 --> 00:36:27.380
What exactly do you mean by that remark?

00:36:27.940 --> 00:36:29.920
Well, I wondered if perhaps there was someone with some pull.

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:32.650
Were you thinking of anyone in particular?

00:36:34.190 --> 00:36:36.250
I understand that a certain Mr. Bruno...

00:36:36.250 --> 00:36:39.220
I thought so. I wonder where we get around to that.

00:36:40.510 --> 00:36:41.970
I simply wanted to find out if...

00:36:41.970 --> 00:36:44.430
There is absolutely nothing between myself and B.G. Bruno.

00:36:45.420 --> 00:36:46.980
I don't suppose you believe that, either.

00:36:47.530 --> 00:36:48.650
Oh, yes, I do believe that.

00:36:49.920 --> 00:36:53.100
I'm getting sick and tired of these stupid fables about me and B.G. Bruno.

00:36:53.440 --> 00:36:57.280
You are? I'm so glad. Oh, where did you meet him?

00:36:57.480 --> 00:36:59.980
What? Oh, we...

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:02.000
He met at a party last winter.

00:37:03.080 --> 00:37:06.050
I understand he was in, uh, Egypt last winter.

00:37:06.870 --> 00:37:10.220
Well, well, Cairo is in Egypt, isn't it?

00:37:11.540 --> 00:37:13.880
Oh, yes. He's been there a long time.

00:37:14.700 --> 00:37:16.580
Well, that's where we met, on the pyramids.

00:37:17.880 --> 00:37:18.620
On the pyramids?

00:37:18.990 --> 00:37:22.270
I mean, near the pyramids, just a little to the left.

00:37:23.550 --> 00:37:26.700
A little to the left?

00:37:26.840 --> 00:37:29.580
It was in Hawaii that Jared met B. G. Bruno.

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:30.800
on the beach at Waikiki.

00:37:30.980 --> 00:37:32.240
It was love at first sight.

00:37:32.460 --> 00:37:34.060
Was she wearing a grass skirt?

00:37:34.280 --> 00:37:35.000
Well, I did.

00:37:35.740 --> 00:37:37.680
Look, I'm trying to give you a great story.

00:37:37.780 --> 00:37:38.920
You're not even taking notes.

00:37:39.270 --> 00:37:40.670
Oh, I can remember it.

00:37:41.330 --> 00:37:43.930
And what I can't remember, I can make up too.

00:37:44.190 --> 00:37:45.920
Oh, please don't be angry, Miss Jones.

00:37:46.020 --> 00:37:48.100
I had to find out about you and this Bruno fellow.

00:37:49.320 --> 00:37:50.100
Well, coming now.

00:37:50.300 --> 00:37:51.860
I'll have to get into my rehearsal clothes.

00:37:52.000 --> 00:37:53.660
Oh, wait, I haven't got half the material I need.

00:37:55.100 --> 00:37:56.220
Will you meet me again tomorrow?

00:37:56.340 --> 00:37:57.560
Have lunch at the aperitif.

00:37:57.740 --> 00:37:58.760
The aperitif?

00:37:58.820 --> 00:37:59.900
Who do you think you are?

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:00.660
BG Bruno?

00:38:02.030 --> 00:38:02.670
Oh, it's all right.

00:38:02.910 --> 00:38:04.730
I've been saving up.

00:38:05.470 --> 00:38:07.210
You don't have to take me to lunch anywhere.

00:38:07.650 --> 00:38:08.830
Would you please zip me up?

00:38:08.950 --> 00:38:13.620
But if you'd like, we could have a bite at that little place across from the theater.

00:38:14.230 --> 00:38:15.270
Janet, you're on.

00:38:21.340 --> 00:38:22.140
One o'clock.

00:38:22.440 --> 00:38:22.940
One o'clock.

00:38:25.850 --> 00:38:29.620
Oh, I promise you won't mention anything about Bruno in your article.

00:38:30.030 --> 00:38:30.550
I promise.

00:38:30.850 --> 00:38:33.290
It wouldn't be quite, quite...

00:38:33.320 --> 00:38:33.480
Quite.

00:38:33.720 --> 00:38:34.780
Janet, you're on!

00:38:34.880 --> 00:38:35.920
Oh, bye.

00:38:37.100 --> 00:38:37.300
Bye.

00:39:03.450 --> 00:39:04.170
Good morning, sir.

00:39:04.960 --> 00:39:06.790
Thank you, sir.

00:39:16.410 --> 00:39:16.890
Good morning.

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:32.400
Good morning, Mr. Dodds, old man. How is your paunch today?

00:39:32.680 --> 00:39:34.520
You must watch that. And how is your paunch...

00:39:34.520 --> 00:39:37.640
Oh, good morning to you. Mr. Dodds, I want to talk to you.

00:39:38.290 --> 00:39:50.980
Mr. Dodds, has it ever occurred to you that this office lacks something?

00:39:52.670 --> 00:39:53.550
No, Mr. Bruno.

00:39:53.830 --> 00:39:57.430
Well, it does. It lacks charm. Everything about it lacks charm.

00:39:57.860 --> 00:39:59.360
You lack charm. Right.

00:40:00.280 --> 00:40:02.140
I'm sure I'm extremely sorry, sir.

00:40:02.490 --> 00:40:04.530
Oh, don't apologize. It's not your fault.

00:40:04.690 --> 00:40:05.990
But we must brighten it up.

00:40:06.480 --> 00:40:08.520
Life, Mr. Dodds, is a sunny thing.

00:40:08.890 --> 00:40:11.930
You can't expect people to work in cold, drab surroundings.

00:40:12.030 --> 00:40:13.690
Look at them. We need something.

00:40:13.850 --> 00:40:17.360
Over there, and over there, and all over there.

00:40:20.180 --> 00:40:23.660
Flowers. That's what we need. Lots and lots of flowers.

00:40:23.840 --> 00:40:25.060
Flowers, Mr. Bruno?

00:40:25.630 --> 00:40:28.980
Certainly. Gay drapes and flowers always help, don't they?

00:40:30.060 --> 00:40:30.420
Do they?

00:40:30.820 --> 00:40:31.920
You've all gotten into a rut.

00:40:31.940 --> 00:40:32.480
That's the trouble.

00:40:32.580 --> 00:40:33.600
This place is like a morgue.

00:40:33.890 --> 00:40:35.070
You must do something about this.

00:40:35.280 --> 00:40:35.880
And this.

00:40:36.770 --> 00:40:37.310
And that.

00:40:43.340 --> 00:40:45.840
It's a lucky year for Janet Jones of the Mercury Theatre.

00:40:46.240 --> 00:40:47.520
Yesterday, a chorus girl.

00:40:47.680 --> 00:40:48.340
Today, a star.

00:40:48.600 --> 00:40:50.300
Tomorrow, a probable bride.

00:40:52.060 --> 00:40:54.820
We mustn't say who the lucky millionaire is,

00:40:55.060 --> 00:40:58.140
but it looks like greeting cards all the way for Janet.

00:40:58.500 --> 00:40:59.680
Give me that.

00:41:07.700 --> 00:41:10.720
Nice man, you're Mr. Paul Trudy, wasn't he?

00:41:11.190 --> 00:41:12.380
Yes, very.

00:41:12.640 --> 00:41:15.320
Lots of charm and very understanding.

00:41:16.660 --> 00:41:16.920
Yes.

00:41:17.440 --> 00:41:17.620
Why?

00:41:19.040 --> 00:41:20.080
Take a look at that.

00:41:25.190 --> 00:41:25.650
Come in.

00:41:27.750 --> 00:41:28.230
Decent?

00:41:30.380 --> 00:41:32.140
When John Frost does something, he does it properly.

00:41:32.220 --> 00:41:32.720
Get a load of that.

00:41:33.030 --> 00:41:33.610
Is it beautiful?

00:41:34.300 --> 00:41:35.000
Well, look at it.

00:41:35.900 --> 00:41:37.100
Yes, what's it for?

00:41:37.420 --> 00:41:38.320
It's for you and yours.

00:41:39.020 --> 00:41:40.420
Me and mine?

00:41:40.520 --> 00:41:41.820
Yes, it's the model for your new number.

00:41:42.490 --> 00:41:44.570
Specially designed for BG's little lady.

00:41:45.210 --> 00:41:46.350
Ought to make him happy, don't you think?

00:41:46.580 --> 00:41:48.380
And ought to make him delirious.

00:41:51.230 --> 00:41:53.630
Look, Mr. Frost, I think that I'd better tell you that.

00:41:53.630 --> 00:41:54.850
Oh, no, honey, not now.

00:41:54.990 --> 00:41:55.350
Later, huh?

00:41:55.640 --> 00:41:56.600
We'll talk about it tonight.

00:41:56.780 --> 00:41:57.320
Over dinner.

00:41:57.720 --> 00:41:58.560
Will you have dinner with me?

00:41:59.180 --> 00:41:59.960
Oh, why?

00:42:00.810 --> 00:42:03.170
Oh, well, whatever the bud is, cancel it.

00:42:03.290 --> 00:42:05.490
And bring Bruno, I mean, Mr. Bruno, along.

00:42:06.160 --> 00:42:08.030
Oh, Mr. Bruno.

00:42:08.190 --> 00:42:09.330
Yes, I want to talk about the show.

00:42:09.610 --> 00:42:12.260
Oh, you can come too. Stops it from being an odd number.

00:42:12.820 --> 00:42:13.600
Charmingly put.

00:42:14.720 --> 00:42:17.280
Well, I'm sure Mr. Bruno would love to come,

00:42:17.400 --> 00:42:19.660
but he's out of town today.

00:42:19.920 --> 00:42:21.080
Well, okay, tomorrow then.

00:42:22.320 --> 00:42:23.660
All right, if he's back.

00:42:23.860 --> 00:42:25.120
Oh, fine. Wonderful.

00:42:25.960 --> 00:42:27.780
Well, little man has a busy day.

00:42:28.600 --> 00:42:29.890
Goodbye now. I'll see you later.

00:42:34.640 --> 00:42:35.900
Do you live under my feet?

00:42:36.000 --> 00:42:36.960
Oh, I'm sorry, Mr. Frost.

00:42:37.140 --> 00:42:38.200
Oh, could I speak to you?

00:42:38.260 --> 00:42:38.800
It's very was.

00:42:38.940 --> 00:42:40.040
Tomorrow, honey, tomorrow.

00:42:40.540 --> 00:42:41.680
Now, which way are you going?

00:42:41.780 --> 00:42:43.970
Oh, that way.

00:42:44.370 --> 00:42:44.690
Good.

00:42:57.580 --> 00:42:59.930
What do you happen?

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:01.480
That's what I call being punctual.

00:43:02.000 --> 00:43:04.440
And that's what I call being contemptible.

00:43:04.580 --> 00:43:09.420
Oh, you mean the new housing scheme?

00:43:09.970 --> 00:43:11.770
You know very well what I mean, your column.

00:43:12.030 --> 00:43:14.450
My col... Oh, yes, my column.

00:43:17.830 --> 00:43:19.990
I might have known that your promise not to print something

00:43:19.990 --> 00:43:22.150
meant just about as much as your phony charm.

00:43:22.330 --> 00:43:24.700
I didn't write this.

00:43:25.620 --> 00:43:26.240
Then who did?

00:43:26.900 --> 00:43:28.920
Well, it could have been anybody, from the editor down.

00:43:30.600 --> 00:43:32.540
You swear it wasn't you?

00:43:32.700 --> 00:43:33.280
I swear.

00:43:33.990 --> 00:43:35.900
Oh, I'm so glad.

00:43:36.620 --> 00:43:38.930
I couldn't believe you'd do a thing like that.

00:43:40.280 --> 00:43:40.700
Couldn't you?

00:43:41.200 --> 00:43:41.980
Well, no.

00:43:44.160 --> 00:43:45.120
I thought you were rather nice.

00:43:46.380 --> 00:43:46.780
Coincidence?

00:43:47.500 --> 00:43:48.240
Good morning, miss.

00:43:48.750 --> 00:43:49.630
What would you like?

00:43:49.790 --> 00:43:50.290
Your usual?

00:43:50.950 --> 00:43:51.370
Oh, yes.

00:43:51.510 --> 00:43:51.950
Thank you, sir.

00:43:52.150 --> 00:43:52.710
And you, sir?

00:43:56.620 --> 00:43:57.420
Talking to you.

00:43:58.040 --> 00:43:59.540
Oh, I'll have the same as the lady.

00:44:00.250 --> 00:44:01.510
Don't you wish to share one, sir?

00:44:01.690 --> 00:44:02.110
I do.

00:44:02.370 --> 00:44:03.250
Anything to drink, sir?

00:44:03.730 --> 00:44:04.150
Champagne.

00:44:05.290 --> 00:44:05.950
Tea, Sally.

00:44:08.480 --> 00:44:10.580
Well, shall we finish the interview?

00:44:11.440 --> 00:44:11.860
The inter...

00:44:12.500 --> 00:44:13.520
Oh, yes, the interview.

00:44:14.560 --> 00:44:16.120
Now, um, tell me.

00:44:16.320 --> 00:44:16.900
Have you...

00:44:16.900 --> 00:44:17.460
Do you...

00:44:17.460 --> 00:44:18.950
A ring?

00:44:19.110 --> 00:44:19.990
Do you wear a ring?

00:44:20.430 --> 00:44:22.290
I'm not engaged, if that's what you mean.

00:44:22.960 --> 00:44:23.380
Congratulations.

00:44:25.340 --> 00:44:26.470
I'm not engaged.

00:44:27.870 --> 00:44:29.970
I started in the chorus when I was six...

00:44:30.760 --> 00:44:34.880
But last winter I couldn't get a job, so for three months I worked as a waitress.

00:44:35.080 --> 00:44:35.640
Last winter?

00:44:36.420 --> 00:44:36.880
Mm-hmm.

00:44:37.120 --> 00:44:39.140
Was that before or after you went to Egypt?

00:44:40.680 --> 00:44:41.080
Before.

00:44:41.400 --> 00:44:43.980
Then you met Mr. Bee-Gee, Bruno, and he fell in love with you at first sight.

00:44:44.840 --> 00:44:46.500
Oh, he did nothing of the sort.

00:44:46.780 --> 00:44:49.240
Must be mad, as well as old and paunchy.

00:44:51.360 --> 00:44:54.180
Would you like to know how I got my first stage job?

00:44:54.380 --> 00:44:55.560
What does the Bee-Gee stand for?

00:44:56.720 --> 00:44:59.980
Oh, the Bee-Gee? Oh, he doesn't...

00:45:00.320 --> 00:45:06.180
me to say he's rather touchy about it touchy old mad paunchy i'll be getting quite a picture

00:45:06.180 --> 00:45:12.020
mr bruno aren't we oh he's really a very nice person that's good where does he live i walked

00:45:12.020 --> 00:45:18.690
into my first audition and i had this piece of music in my hand where does he live who oh of bd

00:45:18.690 --> 00:45:25.280
oh i never can remember the address he always sends one of his cars for me he does yes

00:45:30.120 --> 00:45:31.500
I had no idea it was so late.

00:45:31.620 --> 00:45:32.540
There's his car now.

00:45:32.760 --> 00:45:33.780
I must be going.

00:45:37.840 --> 00:45:39.800
Oh, that's, uh, BG's car.

00:45:39.900 --> 00:45:40.880
I mustn't keep him waiting.

00:45:41.440 --> 00:45:44.080
Please, I have a lot of things to ask you, especially now.

00:45:44.790 --> 00:45:45.530
I'm sorry.

00:45:46.400 --> 00:45:48.820
Can you meet me here tomorrow, same time, Miss Janice?

00:45:49.700 --> 00:45:52.360
All right, same time, Mr. Paul.

00:46:04.160 --> 00:46:06.810
Oh, have you got a mother-in-law, some blackbirds or something?

00:46:07.030 --> 00:46:15.870
That's too high. Better put him back on the table.

00:46:17.130 --> 00:46:28.320
Yes, Mr. Bruno. Don't you think you ought to see Bates now, sir?

00:46:28.540 --> 00:46:29.930
Bates? Oh, yes.

00:46:30.060 --> 00:46:31.620
Bates, show him in, Mr. Dodds.

00:46:37.020 --> 00:46:38.140
You've come in now, Bates.

00:46:38.400 --> 00:46:38.860
Thank you, sir.

00:46:39.000 --> 00:46:44.390
You may talk, Bates.

00:46:44.790 --> 00:46:47.560
Well, sir, I, uh, you picked up a strange young woman

00:46:47.560 --> 00:46:48.740
in Mr. Bruno's car.

00:46:48.940 --> 00:46:49.280
Yes, sir.

00:46:49.320 --> 00:46:51.180
She was terribly late and afraid of losing a job, sir.

00:46:51.840 --> 00:46:52.920
So you gave her a lift.

00:46:53.180 --> 00:46:55.940
A strange female who, for all you know to the contrary,

00:46:56.100 --> 00:46:57.260
might have been a doubtful character.

00:46:57.520 --> 00:46:59.960
And probably was, since you were so willing to ride a

00:47:00.980 --> 00:47:03.260
Mr. Dodds, I see no reason to indulge in personalities

00:47:03.260 --> 00:47:05.550
about a young lady we, um, we don't know.

00:47:05.810 --> 00:47:07.460
As a matter of fact, she was a very nice young lady

00:47:07.460 --> 00:47:08.140
and very attractive.

00:47:08.960 --> 00:47:10.000
I'm quite sure of it.

00:47:10.340 --> 00:47:12.760
And I don't doubt that you made the most of your opportunities.

00:47:13.060 --> 00:47:14.980
Mr. Dodds, I strongly resent your inferences.

00:47:15.460 --> 00:47:18.020
I'm sorry, sir. I was only putting two and two together.

00:47:19.180 --> 00:47:21.140
Bates has already told us that she was a very nice young lady,

00:47:21.180 --> 00:47:21.920
and I know she was.

00:47:23.530 --> 00:47:24.350
I'm sure she was.

00:47:24.490 --> 00:47:26.490
I'm sure you'd have done the same thing, sir, in the circumstances.

00:47:26.730 --> 00:47:27.390
Quite right, Bates.

00:47:27.680 --> 00:47:29.960
All I ask you to do is to find out from Bates just why...

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:32.280
He was outside the stage door of the Mercury Theater yesterday, officer.

00:47:32.440 --> 00:47:33.280
It was about the summer.

00:47:33.840 --> 00:47:35.660
The young lady said she'd come to court as a witness.

00:47:36.970 --> 00:47:39.240
Oh, oh, I see.

00:47:39.630 --> 00:47:41.970
You've used Mr. Bruno's car for your own purpose.

00:47:42.230 --> 00:47:45.510
You've concealed facts and given lifts to strange women.

00:47:45.780 --> 00:47:50.400
I must tell you, Bates, that Mr. Bruno takes a very grave view of the matter.

00:47:51.390 --> 00:47:54.920
Yes, this is a serious business, Bates.

00:47:55.100 --> 00:47:58.160
And I don't like to feel that my employees are deceiving me.

00:47:58.350 --> 00:47:59.980
And therefore, Bates, I...

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:01.860
I think I am voicing Mr. Bruno's views

00:48:02.410 --> 00:48:05.440
when I tell you that we must regretfully terminate your...

00:48:07.450 --> 00:48:10.190
Excuse me, Mr. Dodds. The auditors are here.

00:48:10.450 --> 00:48:13.870
Oh, oh, uh, thank you. Excuse me a moment.

00:48:15.200 --> 00:48:17.240
Yes, Bates, this is a grave breach of trust,

00:48:17.300 --> 00:48:20.550
and I feel impelled, I feel impelled.

00:48:20.650 --> 00:48:24.650
In fact, I insist on doubling your salary.

00:48:27.620 --> 00:48:29.740
I've got my papers. So let that be a lesson to you, Bates.

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:32.280
No, not another word. My decision is final.

00:48:32.700 --> 00:48:33.480
Thank you, Mr. Bruner.

00:48:33.660 --> 00:48:43.580
What are you doing?

00:48:44.010 --> 00:48:45.710
We're taking this scenery away again.

00:48:45.930 --> 00:48:46.850
Who taught you to do that?

00:48:46.950 --> 00:48:48.530
Mr. Johnskill. He's inside.

00:48:49.270 --> 00:48:49.670
Charlie!

00:48:52.080 --> 00:48:53.000
Kevin, you're here.

00:48:53.440 --> 00:48:55.100
Oh, gentlemen, wait a minute, please.

00:48:55.460 --> 00:48:57.440
We open tomorrow. You said you'd give me time.

00:48:57.810 --> 00:48:59.910
Your time's up, and you've broken your word, as usual.

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:03.220
But you don't understand. I've got the richest man in Edinburgh behind me, haven't I?

00:49:03.360 --> 00:49:03.560
Yeah.

00:49:03.880 --> 00:49:06.980
It's too late. We are finished with all your lies and excuses.

00:49:07.180 --> 00:49:08.160
What do you mean, lies?

00:49:08.320 --> 00:49:10.400
It's a question of a complete lack of ethics, Mr. Foss.

00:49:10.500 --> 00:49:12.340
But you heard me phone Bruno, didn't you?

00:49:12.720 --> 00:49:14.480
I'm starring his girl. Isn't that ethics?

00:49:15.630 --> 00:49:16.410
Well, isn't it?

00:49:18.520 --> 00:49:20.320
Fine, Janet. Send her to my office right away.

00:49:20.440 --> 00:49:21.560
Then why don't we see our money?

00:49:21.680 --> 00:49:24.600
Well, these things take time and documents and lawyers. You know how it is.

00:49:24.760 --> 00:49:27.160
Oh, I want to show you something. Just come to my office for a minute, please.

00:49:27.400 --> 00:49:28.260
Just a moment. Come along.

00:49:31.660 --> 00:49:34.150
Janet, Mr. Frost wants to see in his office.

00:49:34.360 --> 00:49:35.400
I'll be right with you.

00:49:35.780 --> 00:49:37.500
Now, this is the new number I'm putting in the show.

00:49:37.980 --> 00:49:40.160
Can't you just imagine the scope you'll have, Mr. Johnsko,

00:49:40.220 --> 00:49:41.000
when you build that set?

00:49:41.790 --> 00:49:42.510
When I build it?

00:49:43.030 --> 00:49:43.650
But of course.

00:49:44.100 --> 00:49:45.500
You don't think I'd be ungrateful enough

00:49:45.500 --> 00:49:47.620
to give it to someone else, now that I have unlimited backing?

00:49:48.040 --> 00:49:50.180
Stand there and ask me to build another set for you

00:49:50.180 --> 00:49:51.460
when I'm here to take my scenery out.

00:49:51.820 --> 00:49:52.460
Why, certainly.

00:49:52.560 --> 00:49:54.000
I'm not the one to bear any malice.

00:49:54.120 --> 00:49:55.880
Well, you get no costumes out of me.

00:49:56.340 --> 00:49:57.920
Did you want to see me, Mr. Frost?

00:49:58.040 --> 00:49:58.940
Oh, Janet, my dear.

00:49:59.120 --> 00:49:59.980
This is Mr. Johnsko.

00:50:00.960 --> 00:50:02.640
I was just telling them about our plans

00:50:02.640 --> 00:50:05.500
and how we're dining tonight with your fiancée.

00:50:06.080 --> 00:50:06.620
With my...

00:50:06.620 --> 00:50:09.400
Yes, how we're going to discuss the final details of the show.

00:50:10.860 --> 00:50:13.860
Oh, yes. Yes, that's right.

00:50:14.140 --> 00:50:15.680
May I ask where you're having your dinner?

00:50:16.460 --> 00:50:18.300
Oh, at the Bon Vivre.

00:50:18.610 --> 00:50:20.270
We'll make a point of being there, Mr. Foster.

00:50:20.410 --> 00:50:22.560
Oh, good. Now can I have my scenery back?

00:50:22.900 --> 00:50:24.480
At the moment, I see no reason why not.

00:50:24.880 --> 00:50:27.270
I hope I feel the same way tonight. Good day to you.

00:50:27.530 --> 00:50:29.470
Good day, and thank you. Oh, wait a minute.

00:50:30.320 --> 00:50:31.780
You can't build a set without the model.

00:50:32.000 --> 00:50:32.940
Oh, thank you.

00:50:33.360 --> 00:50:34.890
Thank you, and goodbye.

00:50:35.990 --> 00:50:37.920
OK, back again.

00:50:44.020 --> 00:50:46.240
Mr. Frost, I'm afraid it's just impossible.

00:50:46.260 --> 00:50:49.120
Listen, Janet, I'm giving you your big break, am I not?

00:50:49.650 --> 00:50:51.030
Now, there's something I want you to do for me.

00:50:51.610 --> 00:50:53.110
Get B.G. Bruno to have dinner with us.

00:50:53.370 --> 00:50:54.730
But I can't, Mr. Frost.

00:50:55.130 --> 00:50:56.710
He's, uh, he's out of town.

00:50:56.930 --> 00:50:57.610
Oh, he's back.

00:50:57.690 --> 00:50:58.890
I read a show in court yesterday.

00:50:59.320 --> 00:50:59.980
Oh, Janet, you'll be.

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:00.740
You'll be saving the show.

00:51:00.840 --> 00:51:02.260
Your whole career depends on it.

00:51:02.440 --> 00:51:03.360
But I can't.

00:51:03.380 --> 00:51:04.280
I just can't do it.

00:51:04.300 --> 00:51:04.800
But you must.

00:51:04.920 --> 00:51:06.100
Everything I have is at stake.

00:51:06.380 --> 00:51:07.700
Think of all those poor kids depending

00:51:07.700 --> 00:51:08.620
on the opening of the show.

00:51:09.170 --> 00:51:09.530
Yes.

00:51:09.790 --> 00:51:11.510
Oh, Janet, you're a sweet girl.

00:51:11.570 --> 00:51:12.310
You're a sweet girl.

00:51:12.350 --> 00:51:13.310
I knew you wouldn't let us down.

00:51:13.510 --> 00:51:14.970
Now go on home and call up B.G. Brunner.

00:51:15.210 --> 00:51:15.850
Hurry up now.

00:51:19.920 --> 00:51:20.620
Aye, we are.

00:51:21.000 --> 00:51:21.800
I got news for you.

00:51:22.870 --> 00:51:23.350
In again.

00:51:26.900 --> 00:51:29.010
Jimmy, he's no good.

00:51:29.010 --> 00:51:29.390
He lives.

00:51:32.360 --> 00:51:34.480
Do you think he'd pass as a millionaire?

00:51:34.760 --> 00:51:37.620
It's no use, May. I can't go through with it.

00:51:38.750 --> 00:51:42.550
Now, look, if you've promised to produce BG Bruno tonight,

00:51:42.610 --> 00:51:44.010
you've got to produce something.

00:51:44.150 --> 00:51:45.510
I'm going to tell Frosty the truth.

00:51:45.780 --> 00:51:48.150
And look over my dead body.

00:51:49.060 --> 00:51:52.260
Now, relax, and come and choose your fiancé.

00:51:54.820 --> 00:51:56.400
But we don't even know what he looks like.

00:51:56.480 --> 00:51:57.920
He's 35 with a mustache.

00:51:58.780 --> 00:51:59.480
How do you know?

00:52:01.260 --> 00:52:06.460
I rang his secretary, said I was doing an article on famous men and their pastimes.

00:52:07.080 --> 00:52:08.360
And what is his pastime?

00:52:08.440 --> 00:52:09.100
His work.

00:52:09.760 --> 00:52:13.420
Oh, pardon me. Then we'd need a serious-looking gentleman.

00:52:15.580 --> 00:52:17.960
How about this one? He looks very rich.

00:52:18.060 --> 00:52:18.920
He's just gone bankrupt.

00:52:21.030 --> 00:52:22.390
Looks pretty hopeless, doesn't it?

00:52:31.300 --> 00:52:31.900
Paul.

00:52:32.140 --> 00:52:33.260
Yeah, I brought you a few flowers.

00:52:33.700 --> 00:52:34.420
A few?

00:52:35.100 --> 00:52:36.640
Oh, Paul, they're beautiful.

00:52:37.780 --> 00:52:38.460
How do you do?

00:52:38.720 --> 00:52:39.400
How do you do?

00:52:40.320 --> 00:52:41.740
Oh, of course, you two haven't met.

00:52:42.000 --> 00:52:42.920
Paul, this is May.

00:52:43.180 --> 00:52:44.260
May, this is Paul Tracy.

00:52:44.700 --> 00:52:45.440
Hello there.

00:52:45.850 --> 00:52:47.610
I've never seen so many flowers.

00:52:47.770 --> 00:52:48.490
Where'd you get them?

00:52:48.650 --> 00:52:49.210
In a shop.

00:52:49.530 --> 00:52:50.250
What did you do?

00:52:50.430 --> 00:52:50.910
Snitch them?

00:52:51.280 --> 00:52:51.660
Snitch?

00:52:51.800 --> 00:52:52.660
I don't understand.

00:52:52.880 --> 00:52:54.360
Don't ever take any notice of May.

00:52:54.820 --> 00:52:56.480
Be a dear and put these in some water.

00:52:58.310 --> 00:52:59.970
Paul, you mustn't waste your pennies on me.

00:53:01.100 --> 00:53:03.220
It's sweet of you, but it isn't necessary.

00:53:03.420 --> 00:53:04.460
Well, I just saw them in the windows.

00:53:04.640 --> 00:53:05.360
I was going down the street.

00:53:05.560 --> 00:53:11.100
They were in a big... here we are.

00:53:19.540 --> 00:53:20.340
Mr. Bruno.

00:53:20.660 --> 00:53:21.740
May, you're mad.

00:53:22.180 --> 00:53:23.480
We couldn't ask Paul to...

00:53:23.480 --> 00:53:24.060
Why not?

00:53:24.490 --> 00:53:26.530
Are you ready to save Janet's career?

00:53:27.040 --> 00:53:29.360
Of course, but how do you know about...

00:53:29.360 --> 00:53:29.960
Do you think...

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:31.640
You think you could pretend to be B.G. Bruno?

00:53:32.650 --> 00:53:34.760
Pretend? No, Paul, I won't allow it.

00:53:34.900 --> 00:53:36.780
But we could get into terrible trouble.

00:53:36.940 --> 00:53:39.620
Why should we? It's perfectly simple.

00:53:40.050 --> 00:53:43.550
All you have to do is have supper with Janet and Mr. Frost and me.

00:53:43.750 --> 00:53:45.830
What could be nicer? Then I'm supposed to be Bruno.

00:53:46.110 --> 00:53:50.430
You see, Mr. Frost wants to meet B.G., and unfortunately, he's out of town.

00:53:50.720 --> 00:53:53.240
Oh, he's out of town. Where is he this time, in Cairo again?

00:53:53.640 --> 00:53:57.570
No, Monte Carlo. Monte Carlo? He really gets round, doesn't he?

00:53:57.730 --> 00:53:59.520
Will you do it? Of course.

00:54:01.530 --> 00:54:04.210
But, Paul, it isn't easy, you know, pretending to be someone else,

00:54:04.370 --> 00:54:05.430
especially a millionaire.

00:54:06.320 --> 00:54:08.000
Do you think you could get away with it?

00:54:08.220 --> 00:54:08.920
I could try.

00:54:09.340 --> 00:54:12.160
Uh, being a little practical, do you have a dinner jacket?

00:54:12.870 --> 00:54:13.210
Yes.

00:54:13.820 --> 00:54:14.560
Is it all right?

00:54:14.740 --> 00:54:17.080
I mean, it isn't one of those shiny green ones.

00:54:17.200 --> 00:54:17.780
Oh, it's rather smart.

00:54:17.920 --> 00:54:18.380
It has a lot...

00:54:18.380 --> 00:54:18.620
Right.

00:54:19.040 --> 00:54:19.700
You're hard.

00:54:20.950 --> 00:54:23.390
Now then, bring it down.

00:54:23.510 --> 00:54:24.430
You've got to be briefed.

00:54:25.300 --> 00:54:25.900
You sit here.

00:54:27.440 --> 00:54:29.980
First of all, if you brew, you must pretend...

00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:31.980
I know everything about the social world.

00:54:32.160 --> 00:54:35.840
Keep talking about your villa at Monte Carlo and your yacht.

00:54:36.020 --> 00:54:36.620
Do I have a yacht?

00:54:36.780 --> 00:54:37.080
Two.

00:54:38.530 --> 00:54:40.810
And remember, you're a wealthy man.

00:54:41.320 --> 00:54:42.460
Don't act like you.

00:54:42.760 --> 00:54:45.670
Act, uh, cynical and, uh...

00:54:45.670 --> 00:54:46.210
Sort of blase.

00:54:46.410 --> 00:54:46.890
Exactly.

00:54:47.510 --> 00:54:48.990
Oh, and you'd better buy a cigar.

00:54:49.190 --> 00:54:50.250
Oh, I don't smoke cigars.

00:54:50.700 --> 00:54:51.440
You don't?

00:54:51.560 --> 00:54:53.520
Oh, but all millionaires smoke cigars.

00:54:53.580 --> 00:54:54.500
All the time.

00:54:54.840 --> 00:54:55.520
Well, I'll try.

00:54:55.760 --> 00:54:56.560
I just hope I'm not sick.

00:54:58.000 --> 00:54:59.980
Paul, it's very sweet of you to do this for me.

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:01.720
Oh, Janet, I'd do anything for you.

00:55:02.490 --> 00:55:04.630
Now, come along, you two. There's no time for that.

00:55:04.810 --> 00:55:06.790
We've got to get ready for zero hour.

00:55:07.000 --> 00:55:08.610
All right. What time do you go into action?

00:55:09.460 --> 00:55:10.700
Pick us up here about 10.

00:55:11.410 --> 00:55:12.690
You better go. We have to hurry.

00:55:15.630 --> 00:55:16.990
Operation Bruno is on the move.

00:55:17.150 --> 00:55:19.450
And from now until then, keep saying to yourself,

00:55:19.490 --> 00:55:21.730
I'm not Paul Tracy, I'm B.G. Bruno.

00:55:22.040 --> 00:55:23.780
I'm not Paul Tracy, I'm B.G. Bruno.

00:55:23.980 --> 00:55:26.080
Oh, that's terrible. Go home and practice.

00:55:26.460 --> 00:55:29.710
You know something?

00:55:30.160 --> 00:55:32.220
I think we've made a great mistake.

00:55:32.580 --> 00:55:32.980
Why?

00:55:33.370 --> 00:55:36.850
He's the most unconvincing B.G. Bruno we could have picked.

00:55:37.270 --> 00:55:38.090
I'm B.G. Bruno.

00:55:38.350 --> 00:55:39.460
I'm B.G. Bruno.

00:55:40.030 --> 00:55:42.970
I'm B.G. Bruno.

00:56:27.840 --> 00:56:29.980
Just look as though you're used to...

00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:30.820
to this sort of thing.

00:56:31.430 --> 00:56:31.950
I'll try.

00:56:32.910 --> 00:56:35.490
I still think we made a great mistake.

00:56:36.040 --> 00:56:36.680
Good evening, Miss Anne.

00:56:36.680 --> 00:56:37.000
Oh, good evening.

00:56:37.160 --> 00:56:38.380
Mr. Frost has a table, I believe.

00:56:38.540 --> 00:56:38.940
Yes, sir.

00:56:39.060 --> 00:56:39.620
This way, sir.

00:56:51.110 --> 00:56:52.530
This is Mr. Frost's table.

00:56:54.690 --> 00:56:56.410
When he arrives, you might tell him where we're sitting.

00:56:56.590 --> 00:56:57.170
Certainly, Mr.

00:56:57.230 --> 00:56:57.550
Thank you.

00:57:00.220 --> 00:57:04.280
You did that very well.

00:57:04.560 --> 00:57:05.480
I thought so, too.

00:57:19.900 --> 00:57:20.580
Good evening.

00:57:20.980 --> 00:57:21.380
Thank you.

00:57:22.660 --> 00:57:24.440
Now, remember, there's nothing to be nervous about.

00:57:24.640 --> 00:57:27.200
And don't talk too much or you'll give everything away.

00:57:27.710 --> 00:57:29.570
And don't forget your B.G. Bruno.

00:57:30.640 --> 00:57:32.720
Well, well, Mr. Bruno. No, don't get up.

00:57:34.080 --> 00:57:35.880
Just wanted to show you how I feel about Scotland.

00:57:36.120 --> 00:57:38.140
When in Rome, do what the Romans do, wear kilts.

00:57:39.240 --> 00:57:41.360
Very pleased to meet you, Mr. Frost. I've heard a lot about you.

00:57:41.500 --> 00:57:42.880
Well, I've been most anxious to meet you.

00:57:47.960 --> 00:57:51.320
Gee just got back from Monte Carlo on his yacht.

00:57:51.480 --> 00:57:54.630
Oh, yes, on my yacht.

00:57:55.250 --> 00:57:58.350
Cigarettes, B.G. Aren't you smoking your usual cigar?

00:58:00.090 --> 00:58:00.710
I forgot them.

00:58:01.050 --> 00:58:02.970
He's a dreadful one for cigars.

00:58:03.090 --> 00:58:03.870
Well, try one of mine.

00:58:04.070 --> 00:58:04.790
No, no, thank you, no.

00:58:04.830 --> 00:58:07.020
Oh, there you are, darling.

00:58:07.580 --> 00:58:08.080
Oh, Maurice.

00:58:08.520 --> 00:58:08.640
Please.

00:58:08.980 --> 00:58:09.520
Maiden, please.

00:58:10.740 --> 00:58:11.260
Thank you.

00:58:12.400 --> 00:58:13.300
Well, what shall we have?

00:58:13.630 --> 00:58:17.140
Uh, to start with, uh, how about some caviar?

00:58:17.480 --> 00:58:17.880
Wonderful.

00:58:18.800 --> 00:58:19.200
Caviar.

00:58:19.300 --> 00:58:19.980
No, not for me, thank you.

00:58:20.040 --> 00:58:20.520
I don't like it.

00:58:21.740 --> 00:58:22.240
You don't?

00:58:22.500 --> 00:58:24.740
No, I think it's very overrated and much too expensive.

00:58:25.250 --> 00:58:28.250
You don't have to worry about that, being a millionaire.

00:58:30.000 --> 00:58:31.990
Well, how about some oysters?

00:58:32.190 --> 00:58:32.930
I'd like some soup.

00:58:33.520 --> 00:58:33.840
Soup?

00:58:34.140 --> 00:58:34.900
He's joking.

00:58:35.120 --> 00:58:36.240
He adores oysters.

00:58:36.710 --> 00:58:37.750
Don't you, darling?

00:58:38.240 --> 00:58:40.360
He's even got his own oyster beds.

00:58:40.910 --> 00:58:41.770
Isn't he silly?

00:58:41.950 --> 00:58:43.850
He's so rich he doesn't know what he has got.

00:58:44.130 --> 00:58:45.630
Well, what do we have to follow?

00:58:46.630 --> 00:58:48.770
Soul, lobster, roast duck?

00:58:49.030 --> 00:58:50.370
Might I have a plain omelet?

00:58:51.840 --> 00:58:52.720
An omelet?

00:58:53.420 --> 00:58:55.340
BG, will you stop joking?

00:58:55.840 --> 00:58:57.200
You order, Mr. Frost.

00:58:57.400 --> 00:58:58.740
BG and I want to dance.

00:58:58.840 --> 00:58:59.880
This is our favorite tune.

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:01.140
Isn't it, darling?

00:59:02.180 --> 00:59:02.960
Excuse us.

00:59:12.520 --> 00:59:14.260
Honestly, Paul, you're not even trying.

00:59:14.600 --> 00:59:15.320
Oh, I am trying.

00:59:15.990 --> 00:59:17.210
You know what the trouble is, don't you?

00:59:17.620 --> 00:59:18.340
No, what?

00:59:18.700 --> 00:59:20.000
You keep on calling me darling.

00:59:20.580 --> 00:59:23.900
Oh, Paul, you just keep your mind on your job.

00:59:24.280 --> 00:59:26.040
And remember, you're B.G. Bruno.

00:59:26.900 --> 00:59:28.000
I am B.G. Bruno.

00:59:32.880 --> 00:59:36.400
We'll finish off with Crape Suzette and bring some champagne, bottles of it.

00:59:36.500 --> 00:59:37.380
Certainly, Mr. Foster.

00:59:38.200 --> 00:59:39.280
Charming man, Mr. Bruno.

00:59:40.260 --> 00:59:40.660
Charming.

00:59:40.920 --> 00:59:42.940
To look at him, you'd never know he was a millionaire.

00:59:43.240 --> 00:59:43.640
Ever.

00:59:44.000 --> 00:59:58.660
The other gentleman dining at Mr. Frost's table.

00:59:58.880 --> 00:59:59.980
He's dancing at the moment with the...

01:00:01.220 --> 01:00:03.860
Oh, that's Mr. Vigi Bruno, sir.

01:00:04.170 --> 01:00:05.450
Thank you. Not at all, sir.

01:00:06.070 --> 01:00:06.850
A moral reformation.

01:00:07.750 --> 01:00:09.270
Mr. Forster stole the truth.

01:00:15.270 --> 01:00:17.410
Paul, please try and say and do the right things.

01:00:17.690 --> 01:00:18.690
I'd do anything for you, Janet.

01:00:19.170 --> 01:00:20.750
Just concentrate on being Bruno.

01:00:20.970 --> 01:00:25.500
Right. Working out beautifully. Johnskill's impressed.

01:00:25.640 --> 01:00:29.970
I can see it. You know something...

01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:30.900
Very amusing, Mr. Bruno.

01:00:31.140 --> 01:00:32.860
There's three friends of mine sitting over there.

01:00:33.000 --> 01:00:34.200
And seeing us dining together,

01:00:34.360 --> 01:00:36.220
I bet they think you're putting money in my show.

01:00:37.000 --> 01:00:39.640
Matter of fact, I've often thought of putting a few thousand pounds into a show.

01:00:40.140 --> 01:00:41.220
Oh, well, uh...

01:00:41.220 --> 01:00:42.880
Darling, this is our other favorite tune.

01:00:42.960 --> 01:00:44.160
We've simply got to dance.

01:00:44.360 --> 01:00:45.660
You'll excuse us, won't you?

01:00:50.140 --> 01:00:51.640
Fine moment to take them dancing.

01:00:51.900 --> 01:00:57.270
Uh, Mr. Frost, I don't think you should try to get BG to put any money in the show.

01:00:57.630 --> 01:00:58.190
Why not?

01:00:58.470 --> 01:00:59.960
Well, uh, he doesn't...

01:01:00.350 --> 01:01:06.940
understand show business. Listen, by the time this meal is over, Mr. P.G. Bruno will be Mr.

01:01:07.100 --> 01:01:13.140
show business himself. I was just trying to live the part. All right, but you overplayed it. I'm

01:01:13.140 --> 01:01:19.360
sorry. You're very sweet, Paul, and I'm really grateful for what you're doing. It's just that

01:01:19.360 --> 01:01:25.560
you're completely wrong. You're nothing like a millionaire. Maybe I should have worn a beard

01:01:25.560 --> 01:01:29.810
or something. It isn't how you look. It's the things you say.

01:01:30.610 --> 01:01:33.190
I'll do anything you say. I'll even smoke one of frost cigars.

01:01:34.700 --> 01:01:35.380
Let's sit down.

01:01:35.780 --> 01:01:38.340
Here they come now. If she asks them to dance again, grab them.

01:01:38.740 --> 01:01:43.640
What an orchestra they have here, eh?

01:01:44.110 --> 01:01:45.530
Yes, makes you want to keep on dancing.

01:01:45.710 --> 01:01:47.150
Well, it isn't good to overdo it.

01:01:47.350 --> 01:01:50.220
Oh, hello, boys. Are you off?

01:01:50.340 --> 01:01:51.420
I thought we'd stop and say hello.

01:01:51.640 --> 01:01:52.680
Before you said goodbye, eh?

01:01:53.660 --> 01:01:55.100
Oh, may I present Mr. B. G. Bruno?

01:01:55.400 --> 01:01:58.540
How do you do? I hear you're taking an interest in our wee show, Mr. Bruno.

01:01:58.780 --> 01:01:59.760
Yes, yes, a great interest.

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:01.720
Then we'll be seeing more of you around the theater.

01:02:01.980 --> 01:02:02.520
I hope so.

01:02:02.860 --> 01:02:04.440
Well, we mustn't keep you from your dinner.

01:02:04.700 --> 01:02:06.720
And don't you worry about a thing, John.

01:02:06.860 --> 01:02:08.880
My boys will work all night on the new scenery.

01:02:09.100 --> 01:02:11.300
Oh, that's fine, Mr. Jansko. Thanks very much.

01:02:11.460 --> 01:02:11.720
Good night.

01:02:11.880 --> 01:02:12.180
Good night.

01:02:12.630 --> 01:02:13.050
Good night.

01:02:13.250 --> 01:02:13.470
Good night.

01:02:13.610 --> 01:02:13.890
Good night.

01:02:16.090 --> 01:02:20.170
Well, you don't know how pleased I am to hear you say that you're interested in our little show.

01:02:20.390 --> 01:02:21.410
Oh, I am. Believe me.

01:02:21.410 --> 01:02:24.630
If you'd care to come to my office tomorrow, I'm sure I could interest you much more.

01:02:25.090 --> 01:02:27.370
My dear Beachy, how are you?

01:02:28.380 --> 01:02:29.020
Hello, Elizabeth.

01:02:29.670 --> 01:02:29.970
I've been...

01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:33.840
I've been trying to catch your eye all evening, but you absolutely refuse to look in my direction.

01:02:35.870 --> 01:02:37.330
May I introduce Miss Jones?

01:02:37.930 --> 01:02:38.730
Miss Thompson?

01:02:39.110 --> 01:02:39.330
Hello.

01:02:39.410 --> 01:02:40.790
And Mr. John Frost, Lady Martin.

01:02:41.110 --> 01:02:42.390
Well, how do you do?

01:02:42.610 --> 01:02:43.270
How do you do?

01:02:43.850 --> 01:02:46.860
John Frost? Don't I know that name?

01:02:46.980 --> 01:02:49.440
Well, I wouldn't be surprised. Do you read Variety much?

01:02:50.100 --> 01:02:50.500
Variety?

01:02:50.860 --> 01:02:53.060
She's broke. I gave her a couple of pounds to do this.

01:02:53.280 --> 01:02:54.400
Is that a new magazine?

01:02:54.640 --> 01:02:56.360
Well, it all depends on what you call new.

01:02:58.430 --> 01:02:59.970
Mr. Frost is in the theatrical business.

01:03:00.030 --> 01:03:02.050
He has a new show opening at the Mercury Theatre.

01:03:02.190 --> 01:03:02.790
You want to see it, Elizabeth?

01:03:02.950 --> 01:03:03.830
Yes, and bring the Duke.

01:03:06.270 --> 01:03:08.450
You must call sometime, BG.

01:03:09.010 --> 01:03:11.550
She's a phony. Paul gave her two pounds to do this.

01:03:12.780 --> 01:03:13.960
It's been so nice to see you again.

01:03:14.340 --> 01:03:15.380
Well, I must be gay.

01:03:16.310 --> 01:03:19.030
It's been delightful meeting you all. Good night.

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:31.240
And Frost in a kilt.

01:03:32.170 --> 01:03:34.710
Poor old Frosty. He really tries, doesn't he?

01:03:34.770 --> 01:03:35.370
Yes, he does.

01:03:40.170 --> 01:03:42.410
Suppose I really had money. I mean, lots of it.

01:03:43.130 --> 01:03:44.610
Would you like me to let Frost have them?

01:03:45.470 --> 01:03:48.270
I think so. I'd like to see him get a break.

01:03:48.980 --> 01:03:50.200
Besides, my break, too.

01:03:50.560 --> 01:03:51.920
At least it will be for one night.

01:03:52.640 --> 01:03:54.440
Those creditors will probably close him up

01:03:54.440 --> 01:03:55.700
when they find out he's pulled a fast.

01:04:01.240 --> 01:04:03.990
I want to ask you something about B.G. Bruno.

01:04:05.000 --> 01:04:06.180
Don't let's talk about him.

01:04:06.540 --> 01:04:07.320
Here, help me down.

01:04:09.260 --> 01:04:10.400
I want to talk about him.

01:04:12.940 --> 01:04:14.450
No, please.

01:04:15.010 --> 01:04:16.070
We've had a row.

01:04:16.290 --> 01:04:19.370
A row?

01:04:20.120 --> 01:04:20.680
You and Bruno?

01:04:22.420 --> 01:04:22.860
Yes.

01:04:24.440 --> 01:04:24.840
What about?

01:04:26.930 --> 01:04:28.090
About you.

01:04:31.600 --> 01:04:33.620
B.G.'s very jealous of you.

01:04:35.460 --> 01:04:38.210
But that's ridiculous. I'll go and see him tomorrow and tell him.

01:04:38.390 --> 01:04:42.470
No, you won't, Paul, please. Thanks for helping out tonight.

01:04:42.690 --> 01:04:44.440
Surely I can call him up and explain.

01:04:45.860 --> 01:04:53.040
Paul, would you be very angry if I told you that something I've been wanting to tell you...

01:04:54.540 --> 01:04:59.030
I don't know B.G. Bruno at all. I've never met him in my life.

01:05:00.090 --> 01:05:00.890
Please understand.

01:05:06.470 --> 01:05:09.410
Janet, look, there's something I want to tell you, too.

01:05:09.690 --> 01:05:12.840
Janet, look, ever since I met you,

01:05:12.920 --> 01:05:14.920
I wanted to dance and sing and climb trees.

01:05:15.180 --> 01:05:16.980
And I got spots in front of my eyes.

01:05:17.580 --> 01:05:19.260
Janet, hello, are you still there?

01:05:19.740 --> 01:05:21.080
Look, look, I must tell you.

01:05:21.240 --> 01:05:21.940
Janet, listen.

01:05:22.810 --> 01:05:28.800
Oh, I was just fixing a few things.

01:05:31.050 --> 01:05:35.160
Nice evening.

01:05:53.900 --> 01:05:57.760
Told you a hundred times, I do not want to speak to the bank.

01:05:57.920 --> 01:05:59.340
What do I have to do, tell you in scotch?

01:06:02.140 --> 01:06:04.600
My dear Mr. Bruno, how nice of you to drop in.

01:06:04.700 --> 01:06:05.320
Sit down, please.

01:06:05.520 --> 01:06:06.280
Well, I can understand a minute.

01:06:06.380 --> 01:06:07.000
It's a very funny thing.

01:06:07.040 --> 01:06:08.080
I was just thinking about you.

01:06:08.520 --> 01:06:10.200
I, uh, I was going through my accounts.

01:06:10.360 --> 01:06:11.400
Then you started thinking about me?

01:06:11.520 --> 01:06:11.800
Yes.

01:06:12.180 --> 01:06:12.880
No, no, no, no.

01:06:12.940 --> 01:06:13.500
I didn't mean that.

01:06:13.660 --> 01:06:16.140
It's just that, uh, I took quite a liking to you last night.

01:06:16.340 --> 01:06:17.340
There's something about you.

01:06:17.460 --> 01:06:18.300
I wonder what that could mean.

01:06:18.320 --> 01:06:19.600
Well, I don't know, but there it is.

01:06:19.740 --> 01:06:21.860
And I said to myself, no matter what inconvenience to me,

01:06:21.980 --> 01:06:23.720
I'd like to let you put some money in my show.

01:06:23.880 --> 01:06:24.760
Well, that's very kind of you.

01:06:24.820 --> 01:06:28.240
Now, Mr. Bruno, you have no idea what a gilt-edge investment this show is.

01:06:28.400 --> 01:06:29.900
It's so simple compared to your business.

01:06:30.250 --> 01:06:32.750
No paper to buy, no greetings to write, no cards to print.

01:06:32.910 --> 01:06:33.950
You just sell seats.

01:06:34.130 --> 01:06:34.950
Well, as a matter of fact, I want...

01:06:34.950 --> 01:06:36.610
Now, if you'd care to invest a small sum...

01:06:36.610 --> 01:06:37.150
No, I wouldn't...

01:06:37.150 --> 01:06:38.370
Uh, say, 3,000 pounds.

01:06:38.470 --> 01:06:38.690
No, no.

01:06:39.000 --> 01:06:39.620
Well, 2,000.

01:06:39.680 --> 01:06:40.000
No, no, no.

01:06:40.320 --> 01:06:42.540
Well, 1,000, I couldn't let you in for less than 1,000.

01:06:42.640 --> 01:06:43.760
Mr. Frost, my mind is made up.

01:06:43.820 --> 01:06:44.940
Mr. Bruno, look at this book.

01:06:45.400 --> 01:06:48.200
I worked it out that we can make this amount every week.

01:06:48.500 --> 01:06:49.180
Clear profit.

01:06:49.540 --> 01:06:53.440
And then there's the television rights and the film rights and records and any number.

01:06:53.560 --> 01:06:56.250
Mr. Frost, once my mind is made up, my decision is final.

01:07:00.760 --> 01:07:01.540
This'll make you laugh.

01:07:02.080 --> 01:07:04.180
You know what I thought that was, looking at it quickly?

01:07:04.640 --> 01:07:06.080
A check for 10,000 pounds.

01:07:08.260 --> 01:07:08.900
It is.

01:07:13.180 --> 01:07:16.300
Frost, there's one condition attached to that.

01:07:16.460 --> 01:07:17.560
Janet must never know about it.

01:07:17.640 --> 01:07:18.600
It's just between you and me.

01:07:18.680 --> 01:07:19.080
Is that agreed?

01:07:19.380 --> 01:07:21.120
Mr. Bruno, as far as I'm concerned,

01:07:21.240 --> 01:07:22.340
I've forgotten you ever gave it to me.

01:07:22.460 --> 01:07:22.800
Thank you.

01:07:27.840 --> 01:07:29.520
As far as you're concerned, you can forget it, too.

01:07:30.800 --> 01:07:31.220
Yes.

01:07:40.030 --> 01:07:41.110
What are you doing here?

01:07:41.250 --> 01:07:42.570
Well, I can't stop.

01:07:42.730 --> 01:07:43.810
I've got a press reception.

01:07:44.010 --> 01:07:44.250
Goodbye.

01:07:44.760 --> 01:07:45.260
Good luck.

01:07:54.160 --> 01:07:54.880
Oh, get me the bank.

01:07:55.040 --> 01:07:56.140
I want to talk to the manager.

01:07:59.050 --> 01:07:59.890
Oh, Janet, my dear.

01:08:02.580 --> 01:08:06.230
Mr. Frost, what was Pa... Mr. Bruno doing in here?

01:08:06.650 --> 01:08:08.570
Well, now, what does a millionaire do best?

01:08:08.790 --> 01:08:10.020
Oh, I forgot.

01:08:11.070 --> 01:08:14.260
Well, get Charlie for me. I want him to go to the bank.

01:08:15.930 --> 01:08:17.450
Mr. Frost, I demand to know.

01:08:18.000 --> 01:08:20.500
Did the man who just left here give you that check?

01:08:21.770 --> 01:08:24.390
Uh, Mr. Bruno and I have a little understanding, Janet,

01:08:24.510 --> 01:08:26.890
and you're not supposed... But he's not Mr. Bruno.

01:08:27.050 --> 01:08:28.830
Oh, now, Janet, my dear. You want me?

01:08:29.010 --> 01:08:29.970
Oh, yes, Charlie, do me a favor.

01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:33.980
Take this check to the bank and tell him to put extra guards around the vaults.

01:08:34.730 --> 01:08:36.090
10,000 pounds?

01:08:36.250 --> 01:08:37.660
Uh-huh. Yes, sir.

01:08:38.340 --> 01:08:41.170
Then take that to the bank.

01:08:41.250 --> 01:08:42.210
Oh, now, Janet.

01:08:42.330 --> 01:08:44.010
You can't. He'll be arrested for forgery.

01:08:44.390 --> 01:08:45.030
Who, me?

01:08:45.860 --> 01:08:47.300
That man wasn't B.G. Bruno.

01:08:47.680 --> 01:08:50.530
He's just a newspaper man, a friend of mine.

01:08:50.960 --> 01:08:52.580
I don't even know B.G. Bruno.

01:08:57.240 --> 01:08:59.670
Say that again, will you? But...

01:09:00.030 --> 01:09:01.250
This time, give it to me slow.

01:09:01.850 --> 01:09:03.610
I've never set eyes on B.G. Bruno.

01:09:03.970 --> 01:09:06.270
But when you insisted that I bring him to dinner,

01:09:06.390 --> 01:09:09.210
I just had to find someone else.

01:09:11.530 --> 01:09:13.310
I'm so sorry, Mr. Frost.

01:09:15.620 --> 01:09:16.360
It's all right, Janet.

01:09:16.830 --> 01:09:17.930
Will you ever forgive me?

01:09:18.680 --> 01:09:21.180
Oh, forget it now.

01:09:21.300 --> 01:09:22.600
Go on back and get ready for rehearsal.

01:12:00.000 --> 01:12:00.280
Thank you.

01:13:01.040 --> 01:13:01.940
We'll be right back.

01:14:00.160 --> 01:14:00.540
Oh

01:16:58.220 --> 01:16:58.720
I love you out there.

01:16:59.330 --> 01:16:59.490
Thank you.

01:17:00.060 --> 01:17:02.900
That phony millionaire is here in the theater, up in a box, look.

01:17:06.160 --> 01:17:08.500
How do you like the nerve of that guy? Go tell the police, quick.

01:17:08.720 --> 01:17:09.640
Police? Where are they?

01:17:09.720 --> 01:17:12.000
Where are they? They're all over the theater. Do you want a map? Come on.

01:17:13.120 --> 01:17:14.620
Mr. Frost, what are you going to do?

01:17:14.700 --> 01:17:16.240
Now, don't you worry your little head about that guy.

01:17:16.260 --> 01:17:17.200
But you don't understand.

01:17:17.400 --> 01:17:20.060
Yes, I understand, all right. Now, hurry up, change your clothes. You'll be late.

01:17:37.230 --> 01:17:38.870
Don't ask questions. Just come on.

01:17:40.660 --> 01:17:56.370
That was exhilarating.

01:17:57.200 --> 01:17:59.160
Oh, you must be mad coming here like this.

01:17:59.460 --> 01:17:59.700
Why?

01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:00.420
Anything the matter?

01:18:00.720 --> 01:18:02.140
You've got to get away from here quickly.

01:18:02.420 --> 01:18:02.820
What for?

01:18:04.420 --> 01:18:05.920
There's a cop at every exit!

01:18:06.220 --> 01:18:07.540
Did you hear that? He's looking for you.

01:18:08.100 --> 01:18:09.700
Hurry, out the window.

01:18:09.960 --> 01:18:12.410
Well, go on. It's all right.

01:18:12.550 --> 01:18:13.490
It drops into an alley.

01:18:13.650 --> 01:18:14.950
I don't want to drop into an alley.

01:18:15.300 --> 01:18:17.040
He just couldn't fly out of that box.

01:18:17.240 --> 01:18:18.920
Why do I have to do everything?

01:18:19.360 --> 01:18:20.520
Here are the keys to my apartment.

01:18:20.660 --> 01:18:21.460
Go there and lie low.

01:18:21.640 --> 01:18:22.980
Well, that's very silly, but I'd like to stay

01:18:22.980 --> 01:18:23.760
and see the rest of the show.

01:18:24.440 --> 01:18:26.440
Don't you realize that half the police in Scotland

01:18:26.440 --> 01:18:27.080
are after you?

01:18:27.200 --> 01:18:28.020
Why are they after me?

01:18:28.510 --> 01:18:29.970
Forgiving Frosty, that phony

01:18:30.300 --> 01:18:30.500
Let me check.

01:19:07.230 --> 01:19:08.010
She's a friend of mine.

01:19:10.090 --> 01:19:10.410
You do.

01:19:10.850 --> 01:19:11.110
Yeah.

01:19:11.470 --> 01:19:13.770
I'm trying to get back in the theater.

01:19:14.010 --> 01:19:15.130
Trying to get back in?

01:19:15.310 --> 01:19:16.190
Are you crazy?

01:19:16.370 --> 01:19:17.630
You've got to get back out.

01:19:19.110 --> 01:19:19.850
Girls, girls.

01:19:20.270 --> 01:19:20.950
Come along now.

01:19:21.090 --> 01:19:23.230
Get out of your dressing gowns and get into your costumes.

01:19:25.440 --> 01:19:26.460
Why, what's the matter with you?

01:19:26.940 --> 01:19:28.720
Get into your costumes.

01:19:32.880 --> 01:19:34.600
Hi. That's better.

01:19:34.840 --> 01:19:38.540
How to get out of here fast.

01:19:39.030 --> 01:19:39.890
Can I get out the other way?

01:19:52.080 --> 01:19:52.800
That's the end of me.

01:20:01.280 --> 01:20:01.460
Thank you.

01:20:32.750 --> 01:20:34.630
I don't want to be a bore, but there's something I must get straightened out.

01:20:35.260 --> 01:20:35.640
Oh, but you...

01:20:35.640 --> 01:20:39.880
Look, that wasn't a phony check that I gave, Frost, because I am B.G. Brunner.

01:20:40.420 --> 01:20:41.780
Now, listen to me, Paul Tracy.

01:20:42.140 --> 01:20:43.320
I've been trying to help you.

01:20:43.480 --> 01:20:47.380
If you don't want my help, all right, but at least have a little consideration for me.

01:20:47.600 --> 01:20:49.000
This is my opening night.

01:20:49.120 --> 01:20:50.000
Oh, I know. I am sorry.

01:20:50.140 --> 01:20:51.580
But it's true. I can prove it.

01:20:51.680 --> 01:20:52.660
Open the door. Have me arrested.

01:20:52.930 --> 01:20:54.170
You know I can't do that.

01:20:54.250 --> 01:20:54.770
Oh, why not?

01:20:55.300 --> 01:20:56.760
Because I love you, you lunatic.

01:20:58.780 --> 01:20:59.320
Say that again.

01:21:02.140 --> 01:21:04.620
Paul, please, please, will you do as I ask?

01:21:04.740 --> 01:21:06.180
All right, but you do know I'm Bruno.

01:21:06.810 --> 01:21:08.050
Will you get out of that window?

01:21:08.230 --> 01:21:08.790
Oh, I'll get out of the window.

01:21:08.870 --> 01:21:10.550
I should go right back in the box and see the rest of the show.

01:21:13.880 --> 01:21:17.630
Sergeant, after the show, I want to hear all that again about...

01:21:17.630 --> 01:21:18.750
about me being a lunatic.

01:21:21.240 --> 01:21:22.020
Oh, now, wait a minute.

01:21:22.140 --> 01:21:24.700
I'm afraid I'll have to ask you to come down to the station with us, sir.

01:21:24.820 --> 01:21:26.100
But, Sergeant, I can expect...

01:21:26.410 --> 01:21:28.300
I'm sorry, miss. Those are our orders.

01:21:31.280 --> 01:21:32.950
Nice work, boys. Lock him up.

01:21:33.090 --> 01:21:33.770
Good evening, Inspector.

01:21:34.110 --> 01:21:37.010
Oh, Mr. Bruno. I'm very sorry about this.

01:21:37.190 --> 01:21:39.130
Now, don't you start. This isn't Bruno.

01:21:39.270 --> 01:21:39.850
Oh, but it is.

01:21:40.150 --> 01:21:42.230
Of course it's Mr. Bruno. I've known him for years.

01:21:43.500 --> 01:21:45.350
You mean, you're really you?

01:21:46.260 --> 01:21:47.940
It's... it certainly is.

01:21:48.080 --> 01:21:53.040
Where is it? It's gone. The check. I've lost it.

01:21:53.100 --> 01:21:53.920
You better find it.

01:21:54.490 --> 01:21:54.850
Johnny!

01:21:55.940 --> 01:21:56.200
Johnny!

01:22:00.730 --> 01:22:01.450
Do you believe me?

01:22:01.850 --> 01:22:02.750
Oh, Paul.

01:22:02.930 --> 01:22:03.630
Janet, George.

01:22:07.060 --> 01:22:07.760
This is terrible.

01:22:08.260 --> 01:22:09.440
Paul is BG Bruno.

01:22:09.680 --> 01:22:10.420
Oh, who cares?

01:22:10.600 --> 01:22:11.840
You've got a number to do.

01:22:19.000 --> 01:22:19.700
Don't bother me.

01:22:19.800 --> 01:22:20.140
Go away.

01:22:20.240 --> 01:22:20.560
Yes, sir.

01:22:20.660 --> 01:22:21.940
Only I found this and I thought...

01:22:21.940 --> 01:22:22.460
My check.

01:22:22.680 --> 01:22:24.460
Oh, you divine, wonderful girl.

01:22:25.110 --> 01:22:25.990
You must have a reward.

01:22:26.130 --> 01:22:26.710
Anything you want.

01:22:27.020 --> 01:22:27.820
Just ask for it.

01:22:27.900 --> 01:22:29.300
Well, I'd like a few words with you.

01:22:29.320 --> 01:22:29.980
Well, you're going to have a hundred.

01:22:30.060 --> 01:22:31.380
Just start talking.

01:22:31.600 --> 01:22:34.380
Well, you see, Mr. Frost, my father is very disappointed.

01:22:34.700 --> 01:22:38.260
He has a lot of excess profits, and he'd be wanting to invest some in this show.

01:22:38.320 --> 01:22:38.880
Oh, fine.

01:22:39.440 --> 01:22:41.370
I don't feel very well.

01:22:41.930 --> 01:22:42.610
Let's sit down.

01:23:03.960 --> 01:23:20.840
Me as I read, as I know.

01:23:37.480 --> 01:23:40.360
Cause a kiss would make it a

01:23:45.150 --> 01:23:46.330
Then there'd be no

01:24:57.260 --> 01:24:58.620
Did you see his face when he thought he'd lost it?

01:25:00.000 --> 01:25:03.730
I get so excited, but then it was opening night.

01:25:03.950 --> 01:25:06.510
You're miles away, aren't you? Where are you, Hoboken, New Jersey?

01:25:07.160 --> 01:25:07.480
Uh-uh.

01:25:08.130 --> 01:25:09.490
Virginia, milking all those cars?

01:25:09.810 --> 01:25:10.150
No.

01:25:10.960 --> 01:25:11.740
On the pyramids?

01:25:12.100 --> 01:25:14.780
Near the pyramids, just a little to the left.

01:25:15.370 --> 01:25:18.270
Oh, yes, where you met that chap with the big paunch and the bifocals.

01:25:19.200 --> 01:25:19.740
That's right.

01:25:20.330 --> 01:25:22.370
I want to ask you something about VG Bruno.

01:25:22.840 --> 01:25:23.800
Don't let's talk about him.

01:25:25.330 --> 01:25:27.710
But I must. There's something I want to know.

01:25:28.190 --> 01:25:28.490
What?

01:25:29.540 --> 01:25:29.960
What is...

01:25:30.060 --> 01:25:31.160
What does BG stand for?
